const e={P3400:["Cylinder Deactivation System Bank 1","P3400 is the bank-level verdict: the engine computer has concluded that cylinder deactivation on bank 1 as a whole does not behave as commanded, without blaming a single circuit. Makers fill it differently. On the 2019 LT4 Corvette, GM compares a manifold pressure model with all cylinders firing against the same model while cylinders are off; 100 failed samples out of 200 give a Type B code.",["Deactivation oil control valve or its screen clogged by debris","Low oil level, wrong grade or overdue oil change","Switchable rocker arm or lifter broken, dislodged or not latching","Oil pressure too high on cold start, e.g. weak relief valve spring","Engine control software needing an update"],["Check engine lamp on","Rough idle or misfire codes on the deactivating cylinders","Ticking or clattering from the valve train","Reduced-cylinder mode no longer used, higher fuel use"],3,1,["P3497","P3401","P3498","P349B","P2652","P341A","P0300"],""],P3401:["Cylinder 1 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit/Open","P3401 points to a broken control path to the solenoid that switches off cylinder 1, a cylinder that GM and Chrysler V8s and Ford's 1.5 l three-cylinder EcoBoost all deactivate. On the 2019 L84 and L86 V8s, GM looks at the low-side output while it is off: over 200 kilohm to ground counts as open, and 20 failures among 25 readings at 250 ms intervals make it a Type B fault.",["Control wire broken or worn through, e.g. by a hot exhaust heat shield","Loose, corroded or oil-soaked solenoid connector","Open coil in the cylinder 1 deactivation solenoid","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on, on GM after the second trip","Engine stays in all-cylinder mode","Slightly higher fuel consumption"],2,1,["P3402","P3403","P3404","P3405","P3400","P3498"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 1 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P3402:["Cylinder 1 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Performance","This code reports that cylinder 1 does not respond as expected when the engine computer switches it off or back on, although the control circuit itself tests fine. Ford lists P3402 in its Variable Displacement Engine monitor for 2020-2023 gasoline engines: it runs continuously during deactivation, entry and exit, between 400 and 4500 rpm and once oil pressure has had about two seconds to build.",["Low oil level, wrong viscosity or aged oil slows the hydraulic switching","Switchable lifter or rocker of cylinder 1 sticking or not latching","Deactivation solenoid valve sticking or its oil screen blocked","Leaking solenoid seal lets control pressure bleed off"],["Check engine lamp on","Shudder or jerk when the engine enters or leaves reduced-cylinder mode","Misfire on cylinder 1 (P0301)","Cylinder deactivation no longer used, higher fuel use"],3,1,["P3401","P3403","P3404","P3406","P3400","P3498","P0301"],"בקרת שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 1 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P3403:["Cylinder 1 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit Low","The engine computer drives the deactivation valve for cylinder 1 through an output stage that checks its own wiring. P3403 means that check found the control line pulled to ground. GM documents it for the L84 and L86 V8s (2019): with the driver off, an impedance below 0.5 ohm to ground counts as a fault, and 20 failures in 25 samples taken every 250 ms set a Type B code, so the lamp comes on after the second trip.",["Control wire chafed against the engine and shorted to ground","Internal short in the cylinder 1 deactivation solenoid","Oil or water in the solenoid connector","Faulty output driver in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on after two trips","Engine no longer switches to reduced-cylinder mode","Somewhat higher fuel consumption"],2,1,["P3401","P3402","P3404","P3407","P3400"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 1 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P3404:["Cylinder 1 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit High","P3404 is the short-to-power counterpart within the cylinder 1 group. GM tests it while the low-side driver is switched on: if the output still shows less than 0.5 ohm to supply voltage, the current has no proper path through the solenoid, and 20 of 25 samples at 250 ms set a Type B fault. The test only runs with at least 11 V at the powertrain relay and about 425 rpm (L84; 400 rpm on the L86).",["Control wire shorted to a supply voltage in the harness","Shorted winding in the cylinder 1 deactivation solenoid","Damaged output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on","Cylinder deactivation disabled","Possible further circuit codes on other solenoids if a shared supply is affected"],2,1,["P3401","P3402","P3403","P3408","P3400"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 1 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P3405:["Cylinder 1 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit/Open","J2012 reserves P3405 for an open control circuit of a separate exhaust valve actuator on cylinder 1. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. The common systems do not need it: in GM's Dynamic Fuel Management one solenoid per cylinder feeds oil to both intake and exhaust lifters, and Ford's VDE only lists intake codes for cylinder 1.",["Broken wire or loose terminal to the exhaust valve actuator","Open coil in the cylinder 1 exhaust valve actuator","Output driver fault in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on","Cylinder deactivation or valve switching disabled"],2,1,["P3406","P3407","P3408","P3401","P3400"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 1 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P3406:["Cylinder 1 Exhaust Valve Control Performance","Where an engine controls the exhaust valves of cylinder 1 separately, P3406 would mean the exhaust side does not follow the command although the circuit checks pass. No manufacturer documents this code publicly.",["Insufficient or degraded oil delays exhaust-side switching","Exhaust lifter or rocker of cylinder 1 not latching or unlatching","Exhaust valve actuator sticking"],["Check engine lamp on","Rough running or vibration in reduced-cylinder mode","Cylinder deactivation suspended"],3,1,["P3405","P3407","P3408","P3402","P3400"],"בקרת שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 1 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P3407:["Cylinder 1 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit Low","P3407 stands for a short to ground in the control circuit of a dedicated exhaust valve actuator on cylinder 1. No manufacturer documents this code publicly, so there are no published thresholds. As an analogy, GM's intake-side code P3403 counts an impedance under 0.5 ohm to ground, seen with the driver off, as a fault. CARB requires such output circuits to be checked for shorts.",["Actuator control wire shorted to ground","Internal short in the exhaust valve actuator","Engine control module output stage fault"],["Check engine lamp on","No change to reduced-cylinder mode"],2,1,["P3405","P3406","P3408","P3403","P3400"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 1 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P3408:["Cylinder 1 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit High","If an engine has its own actuator for the exhaust valves of cylinder 1, P3408 marks a control circuit that reads high, usually a short to battery voltage. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. For comparison, GM checks the intake-side P3404 with the driver switched on and flags under 0.5 ohm to supply.",["Control wire shorted to a supply voltage","Shorted coil in the exhaust valve actuator","Output stage fault in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on","Cylinder deactivation disabled"],2,1,["P3405","P3406","P3407","P3404","P3400"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 1 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P3409:["Cylinder 2 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit/Open","P3409 is the open-circuit code for the deactivation control of cylinder 2. GM uses it on two very different engines. On the 3.6 L V6 (LGX, LGZ) cylinder 2 is one of the two active fuel management cylinders, and an engineering bulletin links P3409 to oil leaking from the rocker arm oil control valve in the camshaft cover. On the L84 V8 with Dynamic Fuel Management every cylinder has a solenoid;",["Oil leaking at the control valve and soaking its connector (GM 3.6 L V6)","Broken wire or loose pin in the cylinder 2 solenoid circuit","Open coil in the cylinder 2 deactivation solenoid","Engine control module output driver fault"],["Check engine lamp on","Oil residue around the valve cover control valve (V6)","No reduced-cylinder operation, higher fuel use"],2,1,["P3410","P3411","P3412","P3413","P3433","P3497","P0302"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 2 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P340A:["Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit Bank 1","P340A is meant for engines that switch the intake valves of a whole bank through a shared control circuit, rather than one solenoid per cylinder. It reports an electrical fault in that bank 1 circuit, without saying whether it is open or shorted. No manufacturer documents this code publicly, which leaves it without known limits; CARB merely demands that outputs of this kind be monitored for breaks and shorts.",["Damaged, open or shorted wire in the bank 1 control circuit","Corroded or loose connector at the bank 1 actuator","Bank 1 intake deactivation actuator with open or shorted coil","Output stage fault in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on","Cylinder deactivation disabled on bank 1","Higher fuel consumption at light load"],2,1,["P340B","P340C","P341A","P3400","P3401"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר — תקלה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P340B:["Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit Bank 2","P340B mirrors P340A for bank 2, the bank that does not contain cylinder 1, so it only applies to V or boxer engines. It marks an electrical fault in a control circuit that switches the intake valves of that whole bank at once. No manufacturer documents this code publicly.",["Chafed, open or shorted wire to the bank 2 actuator","Oil or moisture in the bank 2 actuator connector","Defective bank 2 intake deactivation actuator coil","Engine control module output stage fault"],["Check engine lamp on","Engine runs on all cylinders permanently","Slightly higher fuel consumption"],2,1,["P340A","P340D","P341B","P3497","P3425"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר — תקלה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P340C:["Deactivation/Exhaust Valve Control Circuit Bank 1","P340C concerns a separate electrical circuit that disables the exhaust valves of bank 1 as a group. A fault in its wiring, connector or actuator coil sets the code. No manufacturer documents it publicly, and none of the known production systems needs it: GM's DFM engines feed the intake and exhaust lifters of each cylinder from one shared solenoid, and a GM patent application describes one hydraulic valve per pair…",["Open or shorted wire in the bank 1 exhaust actuator circuit","Exhaust deactivation actuator coil open or shorted","Connector or wiring damaged by heat near the exhaust side","Engine control module output stage fault"],["Check engine lamp on","Reduced-cylinder mode not available"],2,1,["P340A","P340D","P341C","P3400","P3405"],""],P340D:["Deactivation/Exhaust Valve Control Circuit Bank 2","P340D is the bank 2 version of the exhaust-side group circuit: the engine computer sees an electrical fault on the line that is supposed to disable the exhaust valves of the bank without cylinder 1. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. Separate exhaust control matters because a cylinder can only act as a gas spring if its exhaust valves stay shut too;",["Damaged wiring to the bank 2 exhaust deactivation actuator","Faulty coil in the bank 2 exhaust actuator","Output stage fault in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on","Engine no longer drops cylinders at light load"],2,1,["P340C","P340B","P341D","P3497"],""],P3410:["Cylinder 2 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Performance","P3410 covers a cylinder 2 deactivation system that is electrically intact but does not do what is commanded, such as valves that keep opening or fail to return. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. GM checks this behavior on the L84 under its own code P3499, by watching manifold pressure while cylinder 2 should be off; Ford uses the matching cylinder 1 code P3402.",["Oil bleeding past the control valve seal, pressure lost","Rocker or lifter of cylinder 2 not latching","Low or degraded oil","Broken solenoid tip left in the bore keeps a new valve from seating"],["Misfire on cylinder 2, often after a reduced-cylinder phase","Check engine lamp on","Vibration at light load"],3,1,["P3409","P3411","P3412","P3414","P3499","P0302","P3497"],"בקרת שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 2 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P3411:["Cylinder 2 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit Low","P3411 means the control output for the cylinder 2 deactivation valve sees a short to ground. GM lists it for the L84 V8 (2019), whose Dynamic Fuel Management can switch off any cylinder: below 0.5 ohm to ground with the low-side driver off, 20 failures in 25 samples every 250 ms, at least 11 V on the powertrain relay and 425 rpm. It is a Type B fault, so the lamp lights after two trips in a row.",["Damaged insulation lets the control wire touch ground","Cylinder 2 solenoid shorted internally","Faulty engine control module driver"],["Check engine lamp after two trips","Dynamic Fuel Management inactive, engine stays on all cylinders"],2,1,["P3409","P3410","P3412","P3415","P3497"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 2 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P3412:["Cylinder 2 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit High","On GM's L84 V8 each cylinder, including cylinder 2, has a valve lifter oil solenoid bolted into the block valley. NHTSA's description of the system notes these solenoids are driven with peak-and-hold current for fast response. P3412 is set when the control line for cylinder 2 is shorted to supply voltage: GM checks it with the driver on and treats under 0.5 ohm to power as failed, 20 of 25 samples at 250 ms, Type B.",["Control wire shorted to a voltage feed in the harness","Low-resistance coil in the cylinder 2 solenoid","Engine control module output stage fault"],["Check engine lamp on","Cylinder deactivation no longer active"],2,1,["P3409","P3410","P3411","P3416","P3497"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 2 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P3413:["Cylinder 2 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit/Open","P3413 belongs to the exhaust half of the cylinder 2 block and reports an open control circuit for a separately driven exhaust valve actuator. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. The engines known to deactivate cylinder 2, GM's L84 V8 and the 3.6 L V6, switch intake and exhaust valves through one control valve per cylinder and therefore report circuit faults as P3409.",["Open wire or connector to the cylinder 2 exhaust actuator","Actuator coil open","Engine control module driver fault"],["Check engine lamp on","Cylinder deactivation unavailable"],2,1,["P3414","P3415","P3416","P3409","P3497"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 2 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P3414:["Cylinder 2 Exhaust Valve Control Performance","P3414 would be set when the exhaust valves of cylinder 2 do not follow a deactivation or reactivation command on an engine with separate exhaust valve control. No manufacturer documents this code publicly.",["Exhaust-side lifter or rocker of cylinder 2 not switching","Low oil pressure or aerated oil","Exhaust actuator valve sticking"],["Check engine lamp on","Rough running when cylinders are switched off","Deactivation suspended by the engine computer"],3,1,["P3413","P3415","P3416","P3410","P3499"],"בקרת שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 2 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P3415:["Cylinder 2 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit Low","P3415 describes a control circuit for a dedicated cylinder 2 exhaust valve actuator that is pulled toward ground. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. Cylinder 2 itself is a common deactivation candidate: GM switches it off on its 3.6 l and 3.0 l V6 engines (bulletin 21-NA-036) and on DFM V8s, but there one oil control valve serves the whole cylinder, so wiring faults land on the intake-side codes P3409,…",["Control wire of the cylinder 2 exhaust actuator touching ground","Internal short in the cylinder 2 exhaust actuator","Damaged output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on","Cylinder deactivation inhibited"],2,1,["P3413","P3414","P3416","P3411","P3407"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 2 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P3416:["Cylinder 2 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit High","P3416 means the control line of a separate cylinder 2 exhaust valve actuator sits too high, typically because it touches a supply voltage or the coil has shorted turns. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. The closest published test is GM's for the intake-side P3412 on the L84: once the output stage is active, any resistance to supply below 0.5 ohm is a failure, and 20 hits out of 25 lead to a Type B entry.",["Actuator control wire shorted to a supply line","Shorted turns in the cylinder 2 exhaust actuator coil","Engine control module output stage fault"],["Check engine lamp on","Engine stays in full-cylinder mode"],2,1,["P3413","P3414","P3415","P3412","P3408"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 2 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P3417:["Cylinder 3 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit/Open","P3417 flags a broken path in the drive circuit of the cylinder 3 deactivation solenoid. GM documents it twice: its 2007 Displacement on Demand table covers solenoid circuits on cylinder 1, 3 and 5 and needs 30 bad readings in 100 with the engine turning faster than 800 rpm; for the 2019 DFM engine L84, the ECM expects over 200 kohm whenever its low-side output rests, 20 of 25 checks, Type B.",["Broken or chafed wire between control module and cylinder 3 solenoid","Open winding in the cylinder 3 deactivation solenoid","Loose, oily or corroded solenoid connector","Failed output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on","Reduced-cylinder mode no longer engages","Slightly higher fuel consumption"],2,1,["P3418","P3419","P3420","P3421","P349A","P3401","P3433","P3400"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 3 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P3418:["Cylinder 3 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Performance","P3418 is meant for a cylinder 3 deactivation that is wired correctly yet does not respond as requested: the cylinder keeps breathing when it should rest, or fails to come back. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. GM tests the hardware of cylinder 3 under its own code P349A;",["Low oil level, wrong viscosity or aged oil","Lifter or rocker of cylinder 3 not locking or unlocking","Cylinder 3 control valve sticking or its screen blocked","Oil pressure too high or too low for the switching window"],["Misfire code for cylinder 3 (P0303)","Shudder when the engine changes between modes","Check engine lamp on"],3,1,["P3417","P3419","P3420","P3422","P349A","P0303","P3400","P3426"],"בקרת שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 3 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P3419:["Cylinder 3 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit Low","P3419 says the line feeding the cylinder 3 deactivation solenoid is dragged toward ground. The L84 V8 in GM's 2019 OBD documents shows the test: while the low-side output rests, a resistance to chassis ground under half an ohm is wrong, and once 20 out of 25 readings, one every 250 ms, agree, with the powertrain relay above 11 V and the engine at 425 rpm or faster, a Type B fault is logged.",["Insulation of the cylinder 3 control wire worn through to ground","Internal short of the cylinder 3 solenoid to its housing","Oil or water bridging pins in the connector","Defective driver in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp after two drives","Engine no longer drops cylinders under light load"],2,1,["P3417","P3418","P3420","P3423","P3427","P3411"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 3 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P341A:["Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit Performance Bank 1","P341A is the function check behind P340A: the bank 1 intake deactivation circuit is electrically sound, yet the valves do not end up where they were commanded. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. Comparable checks exist under other numbers. GM's LT4 compares a modeled and a measured manifold pressure with and without deactivation and reports the bank result as P3400;",["Low oil level or aged, contaminated oil","Bank 1 deactivation control valve sticking or screen blocked","Switchable lifters or rockers on bank 1 not latching or releasing","Insufficient oil pressure from a worn pump or leaking seal"],["Check engine lamp on","Jerk or vibration when cylinders switch off or on","Misfire codes on bank 1"],3,1,["P340A","P341B","P341C","P3400","P3498"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P341B:["Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit Performance Bank 2","With P341B the controller judges that intake deactivation on bank 2 is not doing its job even though no circuit fault is present: cylinders keep breathing when they should be sealed, or stay sealed after reactivation. No manufacturer documents this code publicly.",["Oil level too low or oil past its service life","Lifter or rocker on bank 2 stuck in one switching state","Control valve on bank 2 sticking or leaking past its seal"],["Check engine lamp on","Rough running, mostly at light load","Misfire codes on bank 2"],3,1,["P340B","P341A","P341D","P3497","P3499"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P341C:["Deactivation/Exhaust Valve Control Circuit Performance Bank 1","P341C covers exhaust valves on bank 1 that ignore a deactivation command while their wiring and actuator coil check out. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. A Ford patent explains why it matters and how to spot it: a sealed cylinder whose exhaust valve keeps lifting leaves a trace in exhaust pressure, and the controller can respond by reactivating the cylinder, blocking further deactivation and storing a…",["Exhaust-side lifter or rocker on bank 1 not switching","Low oil pressure or foaming oil","Bank 1 exhaust deactivation actuator sticking"],["Check engine lamp on","Popping or uneven exhaust note in reduced-cylinder mode","Deactivation suspended"],3,1,["P340C","P341A","P341D","P3400","P3498"],""],P341D:["Deactivation/Exhaust Valve Control Circuit Performance Bank 2","P341D appears once the bank 2 exhaust valves respond wrongly to a deactivation or reactivation request while the electrical side is intact. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. Timing is the critical part: a GM patent application has the exhaust valves stop before the intake valves when a cylinder is switched off and resume before them when it comes back, so that burnt gas is expelled and no fresh charge is…",["Exhaust lifter or rocker on bank 2 switching late or not at all","Oil too thin, too old or too low for fast switching","Sluggish bank 2 exhaust actuator valve"],["Check engine lamp on","Bump or shudder during mode changes","Higher fuel consumption"],3,1,["P340D","P341C","P341B","P3497"],""],P3420:["Cylinder 3 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit High","P3420 reports that the cylinder 3 deactivation control line carries supply voltage where the module expects to pull it low. On GM's L84 the test runs only while the low-side output is switched on: a connection to battery voltage below 0.5 ohm, confirmed in 20 out of 25 samples, sets a Type B code.",["Control wire of cylinder 3 touching a powered conductor","Shorted turns in the cylinder 3 solenoid winding","Output transistor in the engine control module damaged"],["Check engine lamp on","Fuel economy mode unavailable"],2,1,["P3417","P3418","P3419","P3424","P3428","P3412"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 3 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P3421:["Cylinder 3 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit/Open","P3421 opens the exhaust group of cylinder 3 and stands for an interrupted circuit to an actuator that would switch only the exhaust valves. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. Engines that are known to idle cylinder 3, such as GM's LTA and LT2 V8s (bulletin 20-NA-038) and the L84, let one lifter control both valves of the cylinder, so an open circuit there shows up as P3417.",["Broken lead or loose terminal at the cylinder 3 exhaust actuator","Exhaust actuator winding interrupted","Fault in the control module output"],["Check engine lamp on","Cylinder deactivation locked out"],2,1,["P3422","P3423","P3424","P3417","P3413","P3429"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 3 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P3422:["Cylinder 3 Exhaust Valve Control Performance","P3422 would apply if cylinder 3's exhaust valves disregard an order to stop or restart even though the wiring checks out. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. How such a fault can be spotted is shown in patents: Ford patented a way to catch an exhaust valve still lifting after shutdown by its mark in the exhaust pressure trace;",["Exhaust-side switching lifter or rocker of cylinder 3 stuck","Oil level or quality outside specification","Restricted oil passage to the exhaust switching element"],["Uneven running in reduced-cylinder mode","Fuel trim or misfire codes alongside","Check engine lamp on"],3,1,["P3421","P3423","P3424","P3418","P349A","P0303","P3430"],"בקרת שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 3 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P3423:["Cylinder 3 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit Low","P3423 points to a grounded control wire at a dedicated cylinder 3 exhaust actuator. No manufacturer documents this code publicly, and NHTSA's 2025 look at GM's DFM engines shows why: each cylinder has just one lifter oil solenoid, and it feeds both lifters, intake and exhaust, so there is no separate exhaust output that could fail.",["Exhaust actuator wire of cylinder 3 shorted to engine ground","Actuator winding shorted to its housing","Faulty output stage in the control module"],["Check engine lamp on","No switch to reduced-cylinder operation"],2,1,["P3421","P3422","P3424","P3419","P3431","P3415"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 3 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P3424:["Cylinder 3 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit High","P3424 closes the cylinder 3 block and stands for an exhaust actuator control line that is held at supply voltage. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. The L84 from GM shows how far one shared solenoid can be monitored without it: for cylinder 3 the ECM checks a low-side driver under P3417, P3419 and P3420 and a high-side driver under extra codes of its own, yet none of them is exhaust-only.",["Exhaust actuator wire chafed against a supply line","Shorted turns in the exhaust actuator of cylinder 3","Engine control module output fault"],["Check engine lamp on","Engine runs on all cylinders permanently"],2,1,["P3421","P3422","P3423","P3420","P3432","P3416"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 3 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P3425:["Cylinder 4 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit/Open","Cylinder 4 is one of the four cylinders that classic V8 cylinder deactivation shuts off, together with 1, 6 and 7, both at GM (Active Fuel Management) and on the Chrysler 5.7 L Hemi with MDS. That makes P3425 one of the best documented codes in this range. GM's 2019 tables for the L84 and L86 flag an open when the off-state output shows more than 200 kohm, 20 of 25 samples, Type B.",["Solenoid harness chafed through by the exhaust manifold heat shield (5.7 L Hemi)","Open coil in the cylinder 4 deactivation solenoid","Corroded or loose solenoid connector","Control module software needing an update (Chrysler TSB 18-002-25)"],["Check engine lamp on","Engine stays in eight-cylinder mode","Further circuit codes for cylinders 1, 6 and 7 if the shared harness is damaged"],2,1,["P3426","P3427","P3428","P3401","P3441","P3449","P3497"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 4 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P3426:["Cylinder 4 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Performance","P3426 is one of the few performance codes in this range that makers really use. FCA calls it Cylinder 4 Deactivation Control Performance on the 6.4 l Heavy Duty Hemi with MDS; bulletins 18-082-16 and 18-036-20 list it with P3402, P3442 and P3450 and fix it with new PCM software.",["Restricted oil feed tube to the deactivation solenoids (Ford 5.0 l, TSB 26-2093)","Control software needing an update (FCA 6.4 l Hemi)","Low or worn-out engine oil","Deactivating lifter of cylinder 4 sticking"],["Check engine lamp on","Misfire on cylinder 4 or rough running","Drone or shudder at light throttle"],3,1,["P3425","P3427","P3428","P3402","P3442","P3450","P349B","P0304"],"בקרת שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 4 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P3427:["Cylinder 4 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit Low","P3427 is set when the cylinder 4 deactivation solenoid circuit has a path to ground. GM uses it on several 2019 V8s: the DFM engine L84, the AFM engine L86 and the LT4 of the Corvette. Once the low-side output is switched off, less than half an ohm toward ground fails the check; 20 of 25 samples, relay voltage at least 11 V, 425 rpm (L84) or 400 rpm (L86, LT4), Type B.",["Control wire to the cylinder 4 solenoid rubbed through to ground, e.g. by a heat shield","Cylinder 4 solenoid shorted internally","Moisture or oil in the solenoid connector","Damaged driver in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp after two drives","V4 or reduced mode never engages","Further circuit codes on other deactivating cylinders if the harness is damaged"],2,1,["P3425","P3426","P3428","P3431","P3419","P3403"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 4 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P3428:["Cylinder 4 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit High","P3428 means the wire that switches cylinder 4's deactivation solenoid is tied to voltage. GM's bulletin 20-NA-038 lists cylinders 1, 4, 6 and 7 as the ones its AFM V8s switch to V4 mode, which makes cylinder 4 a standard candidate.",["Cylinder 4 control wire shorted to a 12 V feed","Low-resistance winding in the cylinder 4 solenoid","Overloaded output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on","No V4 or reduced-cylinder operation"],2,1,["P3425","P3426","P3427","P3432","P3420","P3404"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 4 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P3429:["Cylinder 4 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit/Open","P3429 stands for an open circuit to an actuator that would switch nothing but cylinder 4's exhaust valves. No manufacturer documents this code publicly, although few cylinders are deactivated as often: GM's AFM V8s (bulletin 20-NA-038), the Hemi with MDS and Mazda CX-5 and Mazda6 four-cylinders with deactivation all idle cylinder 4;",["Open conductor or pushed-out pin to the cylinder 4 exhaust actuator","Exhaust actuator coil burnt open","Control module output not switching"],["Check engine lamp on","Fuel-saving mode inactive"],2,1,["P3430","P3431","P3432","P3425","P3421","P3437"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 4 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P3430:["Cylinder 4 Exhaust Valve Control Performance","P3430 would cover exhaust valves on cylinder 4 that keep opening, or stay shut, against the command while the circuit itself is sound. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. Ford shows both sides of the problem: a Ford patent recognises an exhaust valve opening after shutdown from changes in exhaust pressure and responds by reactivating the cylinder and storing a code, while in practice the 2025 F-150 5.0 l…",["Restricted oil supply to the cylinder 4 switching elements","Exhaust lifter or rocker of cylinder 4 not changing state","Oil too thin, too old or too low"],["Vibration in reduced-cylinder mode","Lean or rich fuel trim codes","Check engine lamp on"],3,1,["P3429","P3431","P3432","P3426","P349B","P0304","P3438"],"בקרת שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 4 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P3431:["Cylinder 4 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit Low","P3431 reports a cylinder 4 exhaust actuator line shorted to ground. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. Cylinder 4 is switched off by Chrysler's MDS Hemi as well as by GM's V8s with AFM or DFM, but each of them runs a single solenoid per cylinder, so their bulletins and tables only list intake-side circuit codes: Ram's 2025 software bulletin 18-002-25 names P3425 next to P3401, P3441 and P3449, and for…",["Cylinder 4 exhaust actuator lead grounded on the block or a bracket","Internal short to ground in the exhaust actuator","Control module driver fault"],["Check engine lamp on","Engine stays on all cylinders"],2,1,["P3429","P3430","P3432","P3427","P3423","P3439"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 4 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P3432:["Cylinder 4 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit High","P3432 is the last code of the cylinder 4 block and denotes an exhaust actuator control line sitting at supply voltage. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. The intake-side counterpart P3428 is well covered: For GM's L84, L86 and Corvette LT4 of model year 2019, a supply path below half an ohm, measured while the low-side stage conducts, is logged as a Type B short.",["Exhaust actuator wire of cylinder 4 in contact with battery voltage","Exhaust actuator coil with shorted windings","Output stage of the engine control module defective"],["Check engine lamp on","Deactivation unavailable"],2,1,["P3429","P3430","P3431","P3428","P3424","P3440"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 4 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P3433:["Cylinder 5 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit/Open","P3433 reports an open control circuit to the deactivation valve of cylinder 5, and GM has used it across three generations. The 2007 V6 with Displacement on Demand, which shut off cylinders 1, 3 and 5, already flagged a short or open after 30 failures in 100 samples at 250 ms above 800 rpm.",["Oil leaking at the cylinder 5 control valve into its connector (GM 3.6 L V6)","Broken wire or spread terminal in the solenoid circuit","Open coil in the cylinder 5 solenoid","Engine control module output fault"],["Check engine lamp on","Oil seepage at the valve cover control valve (V6)","Reduced-cylinder mode no longer used"],2,1,["P3434","P3435","P3436","P3437","P3409","P3400","P0305"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 5 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P3434:["Cylinder 5 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Performance","With P3434 the computer has found that cylinder 5 does not switch off or back on correctly, while the control circuit tests fine. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. GM's L84 runs the equivalent test under P349C: manifold pressure stays too high while cylinder 5 is commanded off, meaning its valves keep working.",["Oil leaking past the cylinder 5 control valve seal","Switching rocker or lifter of cylinder 5 not latching","Solenoid tip broken off in the bore","Low or aged engine oil"],["Misfire on cylinder 5 (P0305)","Check engine lamp on","Shaking after reduced-cylinder operation"],3,1,["P3433","P3435","P3436","P3438","P349C","P0305","P3400"],"בקרת שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 5 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P3435:["Cylinder 5 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit Low","P3435 flags a short to ground on the control line of the cylinder 5 deactivation valve. GM documents it codewise twice: in the 2019 tables for the L84 V8, with under 0.5 ohm to ground in the driver-off state, 20 of 25 samples at 250 ms and Type B, and in an engineering bulletin for 3.6 L V6 engines (LGX, LGZ) where P3435 appears along with P3433 and P3409 when oil leaks from the rocker arm control valve.",["Oil in the cylinder 5 valve connector creating a leakage path (GM 3.6 L V6)","Control wire shorted to ground","Shorted cylinder 5 solenoid","Engine control module driver fault"],["Check engine lamp on","Oil wetness at the valve cover around the control valve (V6)","No fuel-saving cylinder deactivation"],2,1,["P3433","P3434","P3436","P3439","P3409","P3400"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 5 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P3436:["Cylinder 5 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit High","P3436 is the short-to-power code for the cylinder 5 deactivation valve. Publicly it is documented by GM for the L84 V8 (2019), where Dynamic Fuel Management uses a dedicated valve lifter oil solenoid for each of the eight cylinders. The engine computer checks the line while its low-side driver is on;",["Control wire touching a voltage supply","Shorted coil in the cylinder 5 solenoid","Engine control module output stage defect"],["Check engine lamp after two trips","Dynamic Fuel Management disabled"],2,1,["P3433","P3434","P3435","P3440","P3400"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 5 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P3437:["Cylinder 5 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit/Open","P3437 is reserved for an open circuit in a separate exhaust valve actuator on cylinder 5. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. GM, the main user of cylinder 5 deactivation codes (2007 V6, 3.6 L V6, L84 V8), only publishes the intake-side group P3433 to P3436, because its systems switch both valves of a cylinder together;",["Broken wire or connector to the cylinder 5 exhaust actuator","Open actuator coil","Engine control module driver fault"],["Check engine lamp on","Cylinder deactivation locked out"],2,1,["P3438","P3439","P3440","P3433","P3400"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 5 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P3438:["Cylinder 5 Exhaust Valve Control Performance","P3438 describes an exhaust side of cylinder 5 that is commanded to deactivate or reactivate but does not follow, with an intact circuit. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. Two patents show why the exhaust side matters: in a GM patent application one shared valve switches the exhaust valves off, and back on, before the intake valves, so an exhaust lifter that lags breaks that order, and Ford detects an…",["Exhaust lifter or rocker of cylinder 5 slow to switch","Insufficient oil pressure for switching","Exhaust actuator valve sticking"],["Check engine lamp on","Roughness or noise while cylinders are switched off"],3,1,["P3437","P3439","P3440","P3434","P349C"],"בקרת שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 5 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P3439:["Cylinder 5 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit Low","P3439 would report a short to ground in the control circuit of a dedicated exhaust valve actuator on cylinder 5. No manufacturer documents this code publicly, and no threshold is published for it. The closest documented reference is the intake-side P3435, which GM's L84 sets at under 0.5 ohm to ground with the driver off, after 20 of 25 samples.",["Control wire of the exhaust actuator grounded","Internally shorted exhaust actuator","Faulty engine control module output"],["Check engine lamp on","Engine runs on all cylinders only"],2,1,["P3437","P3438","P3440","P3435","P3400"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 5 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P3440:["Cylinder 5 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit High","P3440 closes the cylinder 5 block and stands for a high signal, usually a short to supply voltage, in the circuit of a separate exhaust valve actuator. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. The code only makes sense on an engine with a separate exhaust actuator; a Ford patent, for example, checks via exhaust pressure whether an exhaust valve still opens after deactivation.",["Exhaust actuator control wire shorted to voltage","Shorted actuator coil","Engine control module output stage fault"],["Check engine lamp on","Cylinder deactivation unavailable"],2,1,["P3437","P3438","P3439","P3436","P3400"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 5 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P3441:["Cylinder 6 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit/Open","Cylinder 6 belongs to both classic V8 deactivation groups, so P3441 is a code that real engines set. On GM V8s with Active Fuel Management, which park cylinders 1, 7, 6 and 4, the 2019 tables list it for the L86 truck engine and the LT4 Corvette: with the low-side driver off, more than 200 kohm between output and ground counts as an open, and 20 failures in 25 samples (every 250 ms, from 400 rpm) store a Type B…",["Solenoid harness broken or chafed through (on the 5.7 L Hemi by the manifold heat shield)","Open coil in the cylinder 6 deactivation solenoid","Loose or corroded connector at the cylinder 6 solenoid","Control module software that needs an update (Chrysler TSB 18-002-25)"],["Check engine lamp on","Engine no longer drops to four-cylinder mode","Possibly circuit codes for cylinders 1, 4 and 7 as well if the shared harness is damaged"],2,1,["P3442","P3443","P3444","P3445","P3449","P3400","P3497","P0306"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 6 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P3442:["Cylinder 6 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Performance","P3442 reports that cylinder 6 does not switch off or back on as commanded although its control circuit tests fine. FCA uses it as Cylinder 6 Deactivation Control Performance on the 6.4 l Heavy Duty Hemi with MDS in RAM 2500 to 5500 trucks: bulletins 18-082-16 and 18-036-20 list it with P3402, P3426 and P3450 under a lit MIL and fix it with new PCM software.",["Outdated PCM calibration (FCA 6.4 l, bulletins 18-082-16 and 18-036-20)","Restricted oil feed tube to the left-bank solenoids (Ford 5.0 l, TSB 26-2093)","Oil level too low, wrong grade or worn oil, so pressure builds too slowly","Deactivating lifter of cylinder 6 not locking or unlocking"],["Check engine lamp on","Jerk or vibration when the engine changes between eight and four cylinders","Misfire on cylinder 6 (P0306)","Fuel consumption rises because deactivation is locked out"],3,1,["P3441","P3443","P3444","P3450","P3402","P3426","P349D","P0306"],"בקרת שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 6 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P3443:["Cylinder 6 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit Low","Here the engine computer has found the cylinder 6 solenoid's switched lead pulled to ground. GM spells out the test for its 2019 V8s (L84, L86 and the LT4 Corvette): while the low-side driver is off, an impedance under 0.5 ohm toward ground is a fault, and 20 hits among 25 checks while the powertrain relay supplies at least 11 V store a Type B code.",["Insulation of the cylinder 6 control wire worn through to ground","Cylinder 6 solenoid shorted internally to its housing","Moisture or oil bridging the pins of the solenoid connector","Output stage in the engine control module damaged"],["Check engine lamp on from the second faulty trip","Four-cylinder mode no longer available","P3441 stored at the same time on some GM controllers"],2,1,["P3441","P3442","P3444","P3447","P3497"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 6 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P3444:["Cylinder 6 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit High","P3444 is set when the output that switches the cylinder 6 deactivation solenoid to ground still sees supply voltage while it is turned on, meaning the line has a short to power instead of a path through the coil. GM tests this on the 2019 L84, L86 and LT4 V8s with a limit of 0.5 ohm to controller power, 20 errors out of 25 samples at 250 ms intervals and Type B lamp logic.",["Cylinder 6 control wire in contact with a supply wire in the harness","Shorted turns in the cylinder 6 solenoid coil","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on","Engine runs on all eight cylinders permanently","Slightly higher fuel consumption at light load"],2,1,["P3441","P3442","P3443","P3448","P3497"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 6 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P3445:["Cylinder 6 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit/Open","P3445 is defined for a break in the wiring of a stand-alone actuator that would control the exhaust valves of cylinder 6. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. The engines that deactivate cylinder 6 today, GM's AFM and DFM V8s and Chrysler's Hemi with MDS, publish only intake-side codes for this cylinder (P3441, and at GM also P3443 and P3444).",["Broken wire or loose connector at the cylinder 6 exhaust actuator","Actuator coil interrupted","Output stage in the control module faulty"],["Check engine lamp on","Cylinder deactivation disabled"],2,1,["P3446","P3447","P3448","P3441","P3497"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 6 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P3446:["Cylinder 6 Exhaust Valve Control Performance","P3446 stands for an exhaust valve on cylinder 6 that does not follow a deactivation or reactivation command although its circuit is intact. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. GM watches a closely related failure under a code of its own: on the 2019 L84, P318E (Cylinder 6 Trapped High Pressure Exhaust Charge) looks for an exhaust valve that fails to open and let the burned gas out, recognised by crankshaft…",["Exhaust lifter of cylinder 6 switching late or not at all","Oil pressure too low for reliable switching","Exhaust control valve sticking"],["Check engine lamp on","Knock-like noise or vibration when the cylinder is switched back on","Possible misfire on cylinder 6 (P0306)"],3,1,["P3445","P3447","P3448","P3442","P349D","P0306"],"בקרת שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 6 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P3447:["Cylinder 6 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit Low","P3447 is about a ground fault on the lead of a stand-alone exhaust actuator for cylinder 6. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. GM, the one maker publishing the full set of cylinder 6 circuit codes, switches both valves of the cylinder with one solenoid and reports a ground short as the intake-side P3443: impedance below 0.5 ohm toward ground while the driver is off, 20 of 25 samples, Type B.",["Exhaust actuator wire of cylinder 6 chafed against the engine","Internal short to ground in the exhaust actuator","Damaged driver in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on","Engine stays in full-cylinder mode"],2,1,["P3445","P3446","P3448","P3443","P3497"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 6 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P3448:["Cylinder 6 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit High","If cylinder 6 had its own exhaust valve actuator, P3448 would report its control line shorted to battery voltage. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. A GM patent application on cylinder deactivation switches both sides through one shared hydraulic valve and only lets the exhaust valves go first, off and back on, so it shows no separate exhaust control either;",["Exhaust actuator wire touching a supply line","Shorted turns in the exhaust actuator coil of cylinder 6","Engine control module output stage faulty"],["Check engine lamp on","No switch to reduced-cylinder operation"],2,1,["P3445","P3446","P3447","P3444","P3497"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 6 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P3449:["Cylinder 7 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit/Open","P3449 tells you the engine computer lost continuity in the circuit to the cylinder 7 deactivation solenoid. Chrysler documents it twice for the 5.7 L Hemi with MDS: a 2025 bulletin for the 2023 RAM 1500 eTorque lists it next to a cylinder 7 misfire (P0307) and fixes it with new PCM software, and a STAR case names P3449 first when the driver-side manifold heat shield has worn through the MDS harness at the rear of…",["MDS harness at the rear of the driver-side head worn through by the manifold heat shield (5.7 L Hemi)","Cylinder 7 solenoid coil open","Solenoid connector loose or corroded","PCM calibration needing an update (Chrysler TSB 18-002-25)"],["Check engine lamp on","Engine stays in eight-cylinder mode","Rough idle or misfire on cylinder 7 (P0307) on the 5.7 L Hemi"],2,1,["P3450","P3451","P3452","P3453","P3441","P3400","P3497","P0307"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 7 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P3450:["Cylinder 7 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Performance","P3450 reports that cylinder 7 does not deactivate or reactivate as commanded while its solenoid circuit checks out. FCA lists it as Cylinder 7 Deactivation Control Performance for the 6.4 l Heavy Duty Hemi with MDS (RAM 2500 to 5500, bulletins 18-082-16 and 18-036-20): the MIL lights and a PCM reflash cures it, with an optional calibration that also eases drone and shudder in MDS mode.",["Restricted oil feed tube to the left-bank solenoids (Ford 5.0 l, TSB 26-2093)","Outdated PCM calibration (FCA 6.4 l, bulletins 18-082-16 and 18-036-20)","Locking pins in a cylinder 7 lifter sticking from wear or dirt","Insufficient or aged oil delaying the switch"],["Check engine lamp on","Ticking noise from the valve train","Misfire on cylinder 7 (P0307)","Reduced-cylinder mode switched off"],3,1,["P3449","P3451","P3452","P3442","P3402","P3426","P349E","P0307"],"בקרת שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 7 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P3451:["Cylinder 7 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit Low","P3451 means the switched ground line of the cylinder 7 deactivation solenoid has contact with ground somewhere along its way. GM documents the check for the L84 and L86 trucks and the LT4 Corvette (2019): with the driver off, less than 0.5 ohm to ground, 20 hits in 25 samples taken every 250 ms, Type B, meaning the warning lamp waits for a second faulty trip.",["Cylinder 7 control wire pinched or chafed to ground","Cylinder 7 solenoid shorted internally","Oil or water inside the solenoid connector","Defective driver in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on after two trips","P3449 may be stored as well","No four-cylinder mode, higher fuel use"],2,1,["P3449","P3450","P3452","P3455","P3400"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 7 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P3452:["Cylinder 7 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit High","Unlike the open and ground-short checks, GM can only detect P3452 while the cylinder 7 solenoid driver is switched on, because a short to supply voltage shows up as an output that will not pull low when it should. The 2019 tables for the L84, L86 and LT4 set the limit at 0.5 ohm to controller power and need 20 errors out of 25 samples, Type B. The check therefore depends on the ECM actually commanding deactivation;",["Cylinder 7 control wire shorted to a voltage feed","Low-resistance coil in the cylinder 7 solenoid","Engine control module driver defective"],["Check engine lamp on, often only after longer warm drives","Cylinder deactivation unavailable"],2,1,["P3449","P3450","P3451","P3456","P3400"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 7 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P3453:["Cylinder 7 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit/Open","P3453 is the code SAE assigns to an open circuit in a dedicated exhaust valve actuator for cylinder 7. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. GM's description of Dynamic Fuel Management, published by NHTSA, shows how exhaust control works without such an actuator: the same oil signal unlocks the intake lifter at once, while the exhaust lifter waits until the valve spring load drops on the base circle of the…",["Interrupted wire to the cylinder 7 exhaust actuator","Burnt-out actuator coil","Corroded actuator connector"],["Check engine lamp on","Cylinder deactivation locked out"],2,1,["P3454","P3455","P3456","P3449","P3400"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 7 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P3454:["Cylinder 7 Exhaust Valve Control Performance","P3454 covers an exhaust valve on cylinder 7 that does not switch as commanded, with no electrical fault on its control circuit. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. GM's own cylinder 7 check P318F on the 2019 L84 shows why the exhaust side matters: if the exhaust valve fails to open and release the burned gas, the trapped charge is compressed again, cylinder pressure climbs and the intake mechanism can be…",["Exhaust lifter of cylinder 7 stuck in the unlocked state","Oil pressure or oil quality inadequate for switching","Exhaust control valve slow or sticking"],["Check engine lamp on","Hard knock or jolt when cylinder 7 is reactivated","Possible misfire on cylinder 7 (P0307)"],3,1,["P3453","P3455","P3456","P3450","P349E","P0307"],"בקרת שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 7 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P3455:["Cylinder 7 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit Low","P3455 points to a ground fault on the line that would drive an exhaust-only actuator on cylinder 7. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. On GM V8 engines, AFM and DFM alike, a single lifter oil solenoid serves intake and exhaust of each cylinder, so a grounded line there sets the intake-side code P3451: the low-side driver is switched off, the output reads under 0.5 ohm to ground, and 20 of 25 checks taken…",["Actuator wire chafed through against the cylinder head or a heat shield","Actuator coil shorted to its housing","Output stage in the engine control module damaged"],["Check engine lamp on","Cylinder deactivation locked out","Rough running or misfire on cylinder 7 if the actuator pulls in unbidden"],2,1,["P3453","P3454","P3456","P3451","P3449","P3400","P0307"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 7 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P3456:["Cylinder 7 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit High","P3456 would flag a cylinder 7 exhaust valve actuator whose control line is shorted to supply voltage. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. According to NHTSA's summary of the DFM system, GM drives its deactivation solenoids with peak-and-hold current drivers for fast, repeatable switching, and one solenoid serves both valves of the cylinder, so a short to power is caught under the intake-side code P3452…",["Actuator wire of cylinder 7 shorted to battery voltage","Exhaust actuator coil with shorted turns","Current driver in the control module failed"],["Check engine lamp on","Engine does not enter reduced-cylinder mode"],2,1,["P3453","P3454","P3455","P3452","P3400"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 7 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P3457:["Cylinder 8 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit/Open","Cylinder 8 is not among the cylinders that classic Active Fuel Management or Chrysler's MDS shut off (both use 1, 4, 6 and 7), so P3457 is documented only for newer designs. GM's 2019 tables list it for the L84 with Dynamic Fuel Management, which can deactivate every cylinder: more than 200 kohm with the low-side driver off, 20 of 25 samples every 250 ms from 425 rpm, Type B.",["Wire to the cylinder 8 solenoid broken or chafed in the lifter valley harness","Open winding in the cylinder 8 solenoid","Poor contact at the solenoid connector","Engine control module output stage faulty"],["Check engine lamp on","Dynamic cylinder deactivation inhibited","P3459 may be stored alongside on some GM controllers"],2,1,["P3458","P3459","P3460","P3461","P3449","P3400","P3497"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 8 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P3458:["Cylinder 8 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Performance","P3458 describes a cylinder 8 that does not deactivate or reactivate as commanded although its control circuit is electrically fine. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. GM, the only maker with published cylinder 8 deactivation codes, files this failure under P349F on the L84: during a commanded skip, filtered manifold pressure stays above a threshold, which means the intake and exhaust valves kept working;",["Cylinder 8 deactivation lifter not unlocking or relocking","Oil pressure too low or oil aerated","Cylinder 8 solenoid valve sluggish or its screen blocked","False entry after low voltage while cranking, fixed by ECM update (GM analogue 20-NA-204)"],["Check engine lamp on, sometimes going out again","Shake or roughness in light-load cruising","Misfire on cylinder 8 (P0308)"],3,1,["P3457","P3459","P3460","P3462","P349F","P0308","P3497"],"בקרת שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 8 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P3459:["Cylinder 8 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit Low","When the ground-side control line of the cylinder 8 deactivation solenoid touches ground, the ECM stores P3459. GM publishes this test for the 2019 L84 V8 with Dynamic Fuel Management: driver off, impedance below 0.5 ohm to ground, a minimum of 11 V on the relay feed and 425 rpm, 20 errors in 25 samples, Type B. Some GM controllers log P3457 at the same time.",["Cylinder 8 control wire grounded through damaged insulation","Internal short in the cylinder 8 solenoid","Contamination in the solenoid connector","Output driver in the engine control module damaged"],["Check engine lamp on after the second trip","Engine runs on all eight cylinders at all times","Higher fuel consumption"],2,1,["P3457","P3458","P3460","P3463","P3497"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 8 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P3460:["Cylinder 8 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit High","P3460 reports a short to supply voltage on the control circuit of the cylinder 8 deactivation solenoid, found while the output is switched on. GM lists it for the 2019 L84: under 0.5 ohm between output and controller power, 20 of 25 samples spaced 250 ms apart, Type B, with the same 11 V and 425 rpm enable limits as the other cylinder 8 circuit checks.",["Cylinder 8 control wire in contact with a voltage source","Shorted turns in the cylinder 8 solenoid","Faulty driver in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on","Cylinder deactivation inactive, slightly higher fuel use"],2,1,["P3457","P3458","P3459","P3464","P3497"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 8 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P3461:["Cylinder 8 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit/Open","In the J2012 scheme, P3461 marks lost continuity to an exhaust-side actuator of its own on cylinder 8. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. In the published sources, cylinder 8 is deactivated only by GM's newer V8s (DFM on the L84 and L87, a fixed 2-3-5-8 pattern on the LTA and LT2), and per NHTSA those engines feed both lifters of a cylinder from one solenoid, leaving no separate exhaust wiring to test.",["Wire or plug to the cylinder 8 exhaust actuator broken","Exhaust actuator winding open","Control module output defective"],["Check engine lamp on","Cylinder deactivation no longer active"],2,1,["P3462","P3463","P3464","P3457","P3497"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 8 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P3462:["Cylinder 8 Exhaust Valve Control Performance","With P3462 the ECM would be saying that the exhaust valve of cylinder 8 ignores deactivation commands even though nothing is wrong electrically. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. GM covers the exhaust side of cylinder 8 on the 2019 L84 with its own code P3190, Cylinder 8 Trapped High Pressure Exhaust Charge: if crankshaft jerk, normalized by engine speed, exceeds a load-dependent threshold while the…",["Exhaust lifter of cylinder 8 failing to relock in time","Oil supply to the lifter gallery insufficient","Exhaust-side control valve sticking"],["Check engine lamp on","Vibration while cylinders are deactivated","Misfire on cylinder 8 (P0308)"],3,1,["P3461","P3463","P3464","P3458","P349F","P0308"],"בקרת שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 8 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P3463:["Cylinder 8 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit Low","P3463 would mean that the control line of a dedicated cylinder 8 exhaust actuator is shorted to ground. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. On the only engines with documented cylinder 8 deactivation, GM's L84 and its relatives, one solenoid handles both valves, and GM reports a ground short on it as P3459, testing for less than 0.5 ohm to ground with the driver off.",["Cylinder 8 exhaust actuator wire shorted to the engine block","Exhaust actuator shorted to ground internally","Driver stage in the engine control module faulty"],["Check engine lamp on","Engine stays on all eight cylinders"],2,1,["P3461","P3462","P3464","P3459","P3497"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 8 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P3464:["Cylinder 8 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit High","P3464 is stored once the line to a stand-alone cylinder 8 exhaust actuator sits at a high level, typically a wire touching battery voltage. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. According to GM bulletin 20-NA-038, cylinder 8 is switched off only by DFM engines and by the LTA and LT2, whose fixed pattern is 2, 3, 5 and 8; classic AFM uses 1, 7, 6 and 4.",["Control wire of the cylinder 8 actuator touching a battery feed","Shorted turns in the actuator coil, resistance far too low","Output stage in the engine control module failed"],["Check engine lamp on","Engine keeps running on all eight cylinders, slightly higher fuel use"],2,1,["P3461","P3462","P3463","P3460","P3497"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 8 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P3465:["Cylinder 9 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit/Open","P3465 flags an open circuit to the actuator meant to shut down cylinder 9 or hold its intake valve closed. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders.",["Broken or chafed wire to the cylinder 9 actuator","Open coil in the cylinder 9 solenoid","Loose or corroded connector at the solenoid pack","Output stage in the engine control module failed"],["Check engine lamp on","Cylinder shut-off no longer engages","Slightly higher fuel consumption at part load"],2,1,["P3466","P3467","P3468","P3469","P3400","P3497","P0309"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 9 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P3466:["Cylinder 9 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Performance","P3466 is the plausibility test for cylinder 9: its actuator circuit is electrically sound, yet the cylinder fails to change state when the engine computer commands it. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders. In valve-based systems the switching happens hydraulically;",["Oil level, pressure or quality too poor to switch cylinder 9","Leak at the oil tubes or solenoid pack feeding cylinder 9","Switching lifter of cylinder 9 sticking","Solenoid valve slow or sticking mechanically"],["Check engine lamp on","Misfire count on cylinder 9 (P0309)","Rough running while switching between full and partial mode"],3,1,["P3465","P3467","P3468","P3470","P3400","P0309"],"בקרת שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 9 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P3467:["Cylinder 9 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit Low","With P3467 the control line of the cylinder 9 deactivation or intake valve actuator reads too low, which usually means it is touching ground. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders.",["Cylinder 9 control wire shorted to ground","Internal short in the cylinder 9 solenoid","Moisture in the solenoid connector","Faulty driver in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on","Cylinder deactivation disabled","Possible misfire on cylinder 9 if the actuator stays energised"],2,1,["P3465","P3466","P3468","P3471","P3497","P0309"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 9 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P3468:["Cylinder 9 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit High","P3468 indicates that the control circuit for the cylinder 9 deactivation or intake valve actuator is pulled high, typically by a short to battery voltage that the module notices once it switches the output on. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders.",["Cylinder 9 control wire touching a supply wire","Shorted turns in the cylinder 9 solenoid coil","Output stage of the engine control module damaged"],["Check engine lamp on","Engine runs on all cylinders at all times"],2,1,["P3465","P3466","P3467","P3472","P3497"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 9 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P3469:["Cylinder 9 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit/Open","P3469 is set when the circuit driving a separate exhaust valve actuator on cylinder 9 is open. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders. A distinct exhaust actuator only exists where intake and exhaust valves are switched independently;",["Open or chafed wire to the cylinder 9 exhaust actuator","Exhaust actuator coil of cylinder 9 open","Connector at the exhaust actuator loose or corroded","Engine control module output failed"],["Check engine lamp on","Cylinder shut-off blocked"],2,1,["P3470","P3471","P3472","P3465","P3400","P3497"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 9 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P3470:["Cylinder 9 Exhaust Valve Control Performance","P3470 covers a cylinder 9 exhaust valve that does not follow its deactivation command although the control circuit shows no electrical fault. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders.",["Exhaust switching element of cylinder 9 stuck","Insufficient oil pressure for the exhaust switch","Exhaust actuator sluggish"],["Check engine lamp on","Knock or jolt when cylinder 9 comes back in","Misfire on cylinder 9 (P0309)"],3,1,["P3469","P3471","P3472","P3466","P0309"],"בקרת שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 9 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P3471:["Cylinder 9 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit Low","A low reading on the control line of the cylinder 9 exhaust valve actuator triggers P3471, most often a wire grounded against the engine or body. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders.",["Exhaust actuator wire of cylinder 9 grounded","Internal short in the exhaust actuator","Engine control module output damaged"],["Check engine lamp on","Partial-cylinder mode unavailable"],2,1,["P3469","P3470","P3472","P3467","P3497"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 9 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P3472:["Cylinder 9 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit High","P3472 records a high voltage level on the cylinder 9 exhaust valve control circuit, the pattern of a wire shorted to a supply feed or of a coil with shorted windings. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders.",["Exhaust actuator wire of cylinder 9 shorted to voltage","Shorted windings in the exhaust actuator","Faulty engine control module output"],["Check engine lamp on","Cylinder deactivation switched off by the control module"],2,1,["P3469","P3470","P3471","P3468","P3497"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 9 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P3473:["Cylinder 10 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit/Open","P3473 reports an open circuit to the deactivation or intake valve actuator of cylinder 10, the last cylinder of a V10. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders. The V10 engines known for cylinder shut-off are Audi's 5.2 FSI in the R8 and Lamborghini's Huracán from model year 2016.",["Wire to the cylinder 10 actuator open or chafed","Cylinder 10 solenoid coil open","Corroded or loose connector at cylinder 10","Engine control module driver failed"],["Check engine lamp on","Engine no longer switches to reduced-cylinder mode"],2,1,["P3474","P3475","P3476","P3477","P3400","P3497","P0310"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 10 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P3474:["Cylinder 10 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Performance","P3474 is about function rather than wiring: cylinder 10 should shut down or come back, but measured engine behaviour says it did not, while its control circuit is intact. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders. Audi's R8 V10, one of the few ten-cylinder engines with shut-off, works without valve switching;",["Oil pressure or oil condition not sufficient to switch cylinder 10","Lifter or cam sleeve at cylinder 10 sticking","Oil screen or passage to the cylinder 10 actuator blocked","Leaking seal at the actuator"],["Check engine lamp on","Misfire on cylinder 10 (P0310)","Tapping noise from the valve train"],3,1,["P3473","P3475","P3476","P3478","P0310","P3497"],"בקרת שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 10 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P3475:["Cylinder 10 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit Low","P3475 points to a short to ground on the circuit that controls deactivation or the intake valve of cylinder 10. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders.",["Cylinder 10 control wire grounded through chafing","Actuator of cylinder 10 shorted internally","Water in the actuator connector","Defective control module output stage"],["Check engine lamp on","Reduced-cylinder mode unavailable","Possible misfire on cylinder 10"],2,1,["P3473","P3474","P3476","P3479","P0310","P3400"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 10 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P3476:["Cylinder 10 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit High","P3476 is logged when the control circuit of the cylinder 10 deactivation or intake valve actuator sits at too high a level, usually a short to a battery-fed wire found while the output is active. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders.",["Cylinder 10 control wire shorted to a supply","Cylinder 10 actuator coil with shorted turns","Control module output stage defective"],["Check engine lamp on","Cylinder deactivation locked out for the drive"],2,1,["P3473","P3474","P3475","P3480","P3497"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 10 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P3477:["Cylinder 10 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit/Open","P3477 belongs to engines that switch the exhaust valve of cylinder 10 through its own actuator, and it reports that this actuator's circuit is open. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders. Ten-cylinder engines with shut-off, the Audi R8 V10 and the Lamborghini Huracán, deactivate a bank rather than individual valves;",["Wire to the cylinder 10 exhaust actuator interrupted","Exhaust actuator coil of cylinder 10 open","Corroded actuator connector","Control module output failed"],["Check engine lamp on","Engine keeps all cylinders active"],2,1,["P3478","P3479","P3480","P3473","P3400","P3497"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 10 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P3478:["Cylinder 10 Exhaust Valve Control Performance","P3478 describes a cylinder 10 exhaust valve that does not switch as commanded although its actuator circuit is fine. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders.",["Exhaust switching element at cylinder 10 stuck","Oil pressure too low for the exhaust switch","Exhaust actuator responding slowly"],["Check engine lamp on","Harsh jolt as cylinder 10 is reactivated","Misfire on cylinder 10 (P0310)"],3,1,["P3477","P3479","P3480","P3474","P0310"],"בקרת שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 10 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P3479:["Cylinder 10 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit Low","P3479 shows a short to ground, or another cause of a low signal, on the control line of the cylinder 10 exhaust valve actuator. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders. Engines with ten or more cylinders that deactivate cylinders include Audi's R8 V10, Lamborghini's Huracán V10 and Aventador V12, and Bentley's W12;",["Exhaust actuator wire of cylinder 10 shorted to ground","Exhaust actuator shorted internally","Control module output stage faulty"],["Check engine lamp on","Fuel-saving cylinder shut-off inactive"],2,1,["P3477","P3478","P3480","P3475","P3497"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 10 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P3480:["Cylinder 10 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit High","If the control line of the cylinder 10 exhaust valve actuator is held near supply voltage, the engine computer stores P3480. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders. A ten-cylinder engine has no cylinder 11 or 12, so P3480 is the last exhaust-valve code a V10 could ever use;",["Exhaust actuator wire of cylinder 10 shorted to a feed","Shorted windings in the exhaust actuator coil","Engine control module output defective"],["Check engine lamp on","Cylinder shut-off disabled"],2,1,["P3477","P3478","P3479","P3476","P3497"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 10 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P3481:["Cylinder 11 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit/Open","P3481 marks an open circuit to the actuator for deactivation or the intake valve of cylinder 11, a cylinder only V12 and W12 engines possess. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders.",["Wire to the cylinder 11 actuator broken","Cylinder 11 actuator coil open","Actuator connector at cylinder 11 loose or corroded","Driver stage in the engine control module failed"],["Check engine lamp on","Engine stays on all twelve cylinders"],2,1,["P3482","P3483","P3484","P3485","P3400","P3497","P0311"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 11 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P3482:["Cylinder 11 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Performance","P3482 is the functional check for cylinder 11: the actuator circuit is electrically fine, but the cylinder does not actually go dormant or wake up when told to. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders.",["Contaminated or insufficient oil for switching cylinder 11","Worn or sticking locking pins at cylinder 11","Oil screen to the cylinder 11 actuator clogged","Actuator seal leaking pressure"],["Check engine lamp on","Misfire on cylinder 11 (P0311)","Noticeable shudder when switching modes"],3,1,["P3481","P3483","P3484","P3486","P0311","P3400"],"בקרת שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 11 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P3483:["Cylinder 11 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit Low","P3483 is stored for a low signal on the control circuit of the cylinder 11 deactivation or intake valve actuator, in practice a short to ground. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders. Cylinder 11 exists only on twelve-cylinder engines;",["Cylinder 11 control line shorted to ground","Cylinder 11 actuator shorted internally","Moisture at the actuator connector","Engine control module output faulty"],["Check engine lamp on","Cylinder shut-off disabled","Possible misfire on cylinder 11"],2,1,["P3481","P3482","P3484","P3487","P0311","P3497"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 11 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P3484:["Cylinder 11 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit High","P3484 signals that the control circuit of the cylinder 11 deactivation or intake valve actuator is too high, for example because its wire is shorted to a battery feed and the module detects it when switching the output on. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders.",["Cylinder 11 control wire touching battery voltage","Cylinder 11 actuator coil with shorted turns","Control module driver damaged"],["Check engine lamp on","Reduced-cylinder mode cancelled"],2,1,["P3481","P3482","P3483","P3488","P3497"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 11 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P3485:["Cylinder 11 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit/Open","P3485 is triggered by an open circuit on a separate exhaust valve actuator at cylinder 11. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders. Bentley's engineers say their W12 shut-off leaves both valve sets working, and they rotate the dormant bank to keep it hot;",["Open wire to the cylinder 11 exhaust actuator","Coil of the cylinder 11 exhaust actuator open","Connector at the exhaust actuator corroded","Engine control module output defective"],["Check engine lamp on","Engine no longer drops to half its cylinders"],2,1,["P3486","P3487","P3488","P3481","P3400","P3497"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 11 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P3486:["Cylinder 11 Exhaust Valve Control Performance","P3486 flags a functional problem with the exhaust valve of cylinder 11: the circuit is healthy, but the valve does not reach the commanded state. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders.",["Exhaust switching element of cylinder 11 jammed","Oil supply inadequate for exhaust switching","Exhaust actuator slow to respond"],["Check engine lamp on","Knock when cylinder 11 reactivates","Misfire on cylinder 11 (P0311)"],3,1,["P3485","P3487","P3488","P3482","P0311"],"בקרת שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 11 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P3487:["Cylinder 11 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit Low","P3487 would tell of a grounded control wire feeding a dedicated exhaust valve actuator on cylinder 11. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; cylinders 9 to 12 only exist on engines with nine or more, and J2012 keeps these codes for them.",["Actuator wire chafed through to engine ground","Actuator coil shorted to its housing","Moisture in the actuator connector bridging to ground"],["Check engine lamp on","Bank shut-off no longer offered","Possible misfire on cylinder 11 (P0311)"],2,1,["P3485","P3486","P3488","P3483","P0311","P3497"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 11 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P3488:["Cylinder 11 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit High","With P3488, the cylinder 11 exhaust actuator line sits too high, most often since the wire has picked up battery voltage. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; cylinders 9 to 12 only exist on engines with nine or more, and J2012 keeps these codes for them.",["Control wire of the cylinder 11 actuator touching a battery feed","Shorted turns in the actuator coil","Output stage in the engine control module failed"],["Check engine lamp on","Engine stays on all twelve cylinders"],2,1,["P3485","P3486","P3487","P3484","P3497"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 11 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P3489:["Cylinder 12 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit/Open","P3489 reports that the circuit to the actuator for deactivation or the intake valve of cylinder 12, the highest cylinder number in this code series, is open. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders.",["Wire to the cylinder 12 actuator open or chafed","Cylinder 12 actuator coil open","Loose or corroded connector at cylinder 12","Output stage of the control module failed"],["Check engine lamp on","Engine no longer runs in reduced-cylinder mode","Somewhat higher fuel use on the highway"],2,1,["P3490","P3491","P3492","P3493","P3400","P3497","P0312"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 12 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P3490:["Cylinder 12 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Performance","P3490 concerns the mechanical result on cylinder 12: the actuator circuit passes its electrical checks, but the cylinder does not deactivate or reactivate as intended. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders.",["Oil pressure or quality inadequate to switch cylinder 12","Leak in the oil supply to the cylinder 12 actuator","Locking pins at cylinder 12 sticking","Actuator valve mechanically sluggish"],["Check engine lamp on","Misfire on cylinder 12 (P0312)","Vibration at light load"],3,1,["P3489","P3491","P3492","P3494","P0312","P3497"],"בקרת שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 12 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P3491:["Cylinder 12 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit Low","A ground fault on the control line of the cylinder 12 deactivation or intake valve actuator produces P3491. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders. The Aventador's cylinder deactivation system, introduced in 2012, shuts down one bank of six below 135 km/h, and Bentley's W12 drops one bank;",["Cylinder 12 control wire shorted to ground","Internal short in the cylinder 12 actuator","Water ingress at the connector","Faulty control module driver"],["Check engine lamp on","Cylinder shut-off blocked","Possible misfire on cylinder 12"],2,1,["P3489","P3490","P3492","P3495","P0312","P3400"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 12 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P3492:["Cylinder 12 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Circuit High","P3492 records a high condition on the control circuit of the cylinder 12 deactivation or intake valve actuator, generally a short to a supply voltage seen while the output is commanded on. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders.",["Cylinder 12 control wire shorted to supply voltage","Shorted turns in the cylinder 12 actuator","Engine control module output damaged"],["Check engine lamp on","Engine runs permanently on twelve cylinders"],2,1,["P3489","P3490","P3491","P3496","P3497"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 12 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P3493:["Cylinder 12 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit/Open","P3493 applies to a separately controlled exhaust valve on cylinder 12 and reports that its actuator circuit is open. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders. Bentley's W12 and the Lamborghini Aventador V12 shut off banks;",["Wire to the cylinder 12 exhaust actuator open","Coil of the cylinder 12 exhaust actuator interrupted","Exhaust actuator connector corroded","Control module output failed"],["Check engine lamp on","Partial-cylinder operation unavailable"],2,1,["P3494","P3495","P3496","P3489","P3400","P3497"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 12 — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P3494:["Cylinder 12 Exhaust Valve Control Performance","P3494 is set when the exhaust valve of cylinder 12 does not follow its command although the actuator circuit is electrically intact. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders. Valve-based shut-off traps a charge in the cylinder;",["Exhaust switching element at cylinder 12 sticking","Oil pressure or quality insufficient for the exhaust switch","Exhaust actuator sluggish"],["Check engine lamp on","Jolt or knock on reactivation of cylinder 12","Misfire on cylinder 12 (P0312)"],3,1,["P3493","P3495","P3496","P3490","P0312"],"בקרת שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 12 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P3495:["Cylinder 12 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit Low","P3495 points to a low signal, usually a short to ground, on the control line of the cylinder 12 exhaust valve actuator. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders.",["Exhaust actuator wire of cylinder 12 grounded","Exhaust actuator with internal short","Control module output faulty"],["Check engine lamp on","Cylinder deactivation inactive"],2,1,["P3493","P3494","P3496","P3491","P3497"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 12 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P3496:["Cylinder 12 Exhaust Valve Control Circuit High","P3496 is the final code of the per-cylinder valve block: it marks the cylinder 12 exhaust valve control circuit as too high, typically a short to battery voltage or a coil with shorted turns. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; J2012 reserves the codes for cylinders 9 to 12 for engines with more than eight cylinders.",["Exhaust actuator wire of cylinder 12 shorted to battery voltage","Shorted turns in the exhaust actuator coil","Engine control module output damaged"],["Check engine lamp on","Cylinder shut-off disabled"],2,1,["P3493","P3494","P3495","P3492","P3497"],"שסתום פליטת צילינדר‏ 12 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P3497:["Cylinder Deactivation System Bank 2","P3497 is the bank 2 counterpart of P3400: the control unit concludes that deactivation on the bank that lacks cylinder 1 is failing as a whole, and it blames no single cylinder circuit. Honda's VCM V6 links it to rocker arm oil pressure switch C (P3400 belongs to switch B);",["Low oil level, wrong grade or overdue oil change on bank 2","Excess oil pressure on cold start, e.g. weak relief valve spring","Switchable rocker arm or lifter on bank 2 sticking or not latching","Rocker arm oil pressure switch of bank 2 reporting wrongly","Engine control software needing an update"],["Check engine lamp on","Misfire codes on bank 2 cylinders, mostly after a cold start","Rough idle while the engine warms up","Reduced-cylinder mode no longer used, higher fuel use"],3,1,["P3400","P3409","P3410","P0300","P2652"],""],P3498:["Cylinder 1 Deactivation/Intake Valve Performance","P3498 flags a mechanical failure on cylinder 1: the control unit commanded it off, but its valves kept opening. This differs from P3402, which concerns the control side, and from the wiring codes P3401, P3403 and P3404. GM runs the check on its 5.3 l L84 and 6.2 l L87 Dynamic Fuel Management V8s by watching filtered manifold pressure every 90 crank degrees;",["Switchable rocker arm of cylinder 1 dropped out or broken (Mazda)","Deactivation lifter of cylinder 1 stays locked (GM DFM)","Lifter oil solenoid of cylinder 1 sticking or with protruding pole piece","Overdue oil changes or wrong oil grade"],["Check engine lamp on","Rough idle or misfire on cylinder 1 (P0301)","Clatter from the cylinder head and loss of power","Cylinder deactivation no longer used, higher fuel use"],3,1,["P3402","P3401","P3400","P349B","P3499","P0301","P0340"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 1 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P3499:["Cylinder 2 Deactivation/Intake Valve Performance","P3499 reports that cylinder 2 did not stop exchanging gas when told to deactivate. On GM's DFM V8s (L84, L87) one oil solenoid in the lifter valley feeds both lifters of the cylinder; oil pressure pushes spring-loaded pins inward which lets the outer lifter shell ride the cam while the valve remains closed.",["Locking pins in the cylinder 2 lifters do not retract","Lifter oil solenoid of cylinder 2 not delivering oil pressure","Low, aerated or degraded oil","Code stored without a real fault, ECM software update needed"],["Check engine lamp on","Higher fuel consumption because cylinder 2 is no longer skipped","Ticking from the lifter area"],3,1,["P3410","P3409","P3411","P3412","P3498","P349A","P0302"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 2 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P349A:["Cylinder 3 Deactivation/Intake Valve Performance","P349A states that cylinder 3 kept its valves working while the engine computer had switched it off. GM picks this up on its L84 and L87 V8s through manifold pressure that stays too high during the skipped strokes, Type B after 22 failed checks out of 25. Not every stored P349A means a worn lifter.",["Voltage dip at cranking disabled the outputs, ECM software outdated","Deactivation lifter of cylinder 3 does not unlock","Lifter oil solenoid of cylinder 3 sticking","Low or aged oil slowing the switching"],["Code stored in history with no noticeable concern","Check engine lamp on if the fault is real","Ticking noise or higher fuel use"],3,1,["P3418","P3417","P3419","P3420","P3499","P349B","P0303"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 3 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P349B:["Cylinder 4 Deactivation/Intake Valve Performance","P349B is set when cylinder 4 fails to shut its valves on command. On Mazda's 2.5 l Skyactiv-G with cylinder deactivation (CX-5 and Mazda6, 2018-2019), cylinders 1 and 4 can be switched off; service alerts SA-041/18 and SA-022/19 tie P349B, P3498, P3400, P0304 and P0340 to a rocker arm that fell out of place or broke.",["Rocker arm of cylinder 4 fallen out of place or broken (Mazda)","Long oil change intervals or unsuitable oil","Deactivation lifter of cylinder 4 stuck locked (GM DFM)","Oil control solenoid of cylinder 4 faulty"],["Rough idle and misfire on cylinder 4 (P0304)","Clatter or knocking from the valve cover area","Lack of power","Check engine lamp on"],4,1,["P3426","P3425","P3400","P3498","P349A","P349C","P0304","P0340"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 4 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P349C:["Cylinder 5 Deactivation/Intake Valve Performance","P349C means that cylinder 5 stayed active although the engine computer had requested a skip. GM documents it for its Dynamic Fuel Management V8s (L84 with 5.3 l, L87 with 6.2 l), where every cylinder may be skipped; the classic AFM V8s rest only cylinders 1, 7, 6 and 4. Detection compares filtered manifold pressure with a deactivation threshold, and a Type B code follows after 22 failures out of 25.",["Lifter oil solenoid of cylinder 5 faulty, pole piece protruding","Lifters of cylinder 5 do not unlock","Dirt in the oil blocking the solenoid or lifter bores"],["Check engine lamp on","Engine no longer skips cylinders, fuel use rises","Vibration at light load"],3,1,["P3434","P3433","P3435","P3436","P349B","P349D","P0305"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 5 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P349D:["Cylinder 6 Deactivation/Intake Valve Performance","P349D indicates that cylinder 6 drew in and pushed out air during events in which it should have stayed sealed. The test logic rests on a simple effect: every intake stroke leaves a dip in manifold pressure, so a resting cylinder should leave none. Ford's patent US8667835B2 and Delphi's US7314034B1 describe tracking these pulses event by event.",["Locking pins of the cylinder 6 lifters do not release","Oil solenoid of cylinder 6 sticking","Low oil level or degraded oil","Intake leak or MAP sensor fault distorting the pressure pulses"],["Check engine lamp on","Higher fuel use in light-load cruising","Ticking from the engine valley"],3,1,["P3442","P3441","P3400","P349C","P349E","P0306","P0106"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 6 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P349E:["Cylinder 7 Deactivation/Intake Valve Performance","P349E covers cylinder 7: deactivation was commanded, yet the cylinder kept its valve events. In GM's DFM design the intake lifter is unlocked first, while the exhaust lifter can only release once its cam lobe is back on the base circle; a sluggish pin therefore tends to leave the exhaust side working.",["Sluggish locking pin, mostly in the exhaust lifter of cylinder 7","Oil solenoid of cylinder 7 not opening fully","Low, thin or aerated oil"],["Ticking from the valve train","Check engine lamp on","Cylinder deactivation inhibited, higher consumption"],3,1,["P3450","P3449","P3451","P3452","P349D","P349F","P0307"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 7 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P349F:["Cylinder 8 Deactivation/Intake Valve Performance","P349F reports that cylinder 8 failed to go quiet when commanded. California's OBD rule requires makers to analyse every plausible hydraulic or mechanical failure of variable valve systems and mentions, among its examples, a lift-mechanism pin of one cylinder that will not shift; codes like this one follow from that duty.",["Lifter of cylinder 8 stuck in its locked state","Weak or sticking oil solenoid of cylinder 8","Sludge or debris in the lifter oil passages","Stored after a voltage dip at cranking, ECM software update needed"],["Check engine lamp on after two trips","Engine stays on all cylinders, fuel use rises","Ticking noise at idle"],3,1,["P3458","P3457","P349E","P34A0","P3400","P0308"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 8 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P34A0:["Cylinder 9 Deactivation/Intake Valve Performance","P34A0 is reserved for a cylinder 9 that keeps its valves moving after the engine computer has ordered it off, which presumes an engine with at least nine cylinders and per-cylinder valve switching. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. The twelve-cylinder engines with deactivation found so far work bank by bank;",["Switching lifter or rocker of cylinder 9 stuck","Oil control valve for the deactivation not switching","Low or degraded oil"],["Check engine lamp on","Rough running in reduced-cylinder mode","Higher fuel use"],4,1,["P3466","P3465","P349F","P34A1","P0309"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 9 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P34A1:["Cylinder 10 Deactivation/Intake Valve Performance","P34A1 would mean that cylinder 10 kept opening its valves while it was supposed to be deactivated. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; it only makes sense on V10, V12 or W12 engines. Lamborghini, for instance, gave the Aventador LP 700-4 a Cylinder Deactivation System that rests one bank at speeds under 135 km/h, but no public diagnostic table lists P34A1.",["Switching element of cylinder 10 not unlocking","Deactivation oil control valve sticking","Oil level too low or oil aged"],["Check engine lamp on","Reduced-cylinder mode no longer offered","Uneven running at low load"],4,1,["P3474","P3473","P34A0","P34A2","P0310"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 10 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P34A2:["Cylinder 11 Deactivation/Intake Valve Performance","P34A2 names a mechanical deactivation fault on cylinder 11: the valves continued to operate although the cylinder had been switched off. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. The nearest production example is the Active Cylinder Control that Mercedes fitted to the 5.8 l V12 of the CL 600 and S 600 from 2001; it idled one bank and uncoupled its exhaust valves by means of two solenoids;",["Valve switching element of cylinder 11 jammed","Oil pressure supply to the switching parts disturbed","Low or degraded oil"],["Check engine lamp on","Rough running when one bank is shut down","Higher fuel use"],4,1,["P3482","P3481","P34A1","P34A3","P0311"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 11 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P34A3:["Cylinder 12 Deactivation/Intake Valve Performance","P34A3 closes the series at the twelfth cylinder: cylinder 12 was commanded to deactivate, but its valves did not stop. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. A dedicated check is needed because CARB's misfire definition excludes cylinders that are deliberately shut off, so the misfire monitor will not flag a skipped cylinder that still pumps air without fuel.",["Lifter or rocker switching element of cylinder 12 stuck","Oil control valve of the deactivation sticking","Low or aged oil"],["Check engine lamp on","Rough running at light load","Higher fuel use"],4,1,["P3490","P3489","P34A2","P34A0","P0312"],"שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר‏ 12 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P34A4:["A Camshaft Position Actuator Temperature Sensor Circuit Bank 1","P34A4 flags an electrical problem of any kind in the temperature sensor circuit of intake camshaft actuator A on bank 1: a wire broken somewhere, a plug that has worked loose, or a value no valid window accepts. Such a sensor belongs to electrically driven phasers; an Aisin patent places it on the motor driver board and reduces motor current once that board stays hot.",["Plug at the actuator loose or corroded, sensor wire broken","Temperature sensor in the actuator or its electronics failed","Fault in the module that drives the electric phaser"],["Check engine light on","Intake cam phasing on bank 1 restricted or held in its base position","Often no noticeable change while driving"],2,3,["P34A5","P34A6","P34A7","P34A8","P34B4"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 1)"],P34A5:["A Camshaft Position Actuator Temperature Sensor Range/Performance Bank 1","P34A5 means the temperature reported for intake cam actuator A on bank 1 passes the electrical checks yet makes no sense. Nissan describes the code for the 2018 Pathfinder (R52) and the Infiniti QX60 built before 18 December 2017: the MIL came on after starts at ambient temperatures around or below 0 °C.",["Software of the electric valve timing module (Nissan 2018: cold-start false alarm)","Temperature sensor drifting out of its expected range","Intermittent contact at the actuator plug"],["Check engine light on, often after a cold start","Usually no driveability complaint"],2,3,["P34A4","P34A6","P34A7","P34A9","P0011"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 1)"],P34A6:["A Camshaft Position Actuator Temperature Sensor Circuit Low Bank 1","With P34A6 the temperature signal from the intake cam actuator on bank 1 sits under its minimum. No source available to us names the sensor type. If it is the usual NTC thermistor, low voltage corresponds to high temperature, so a signal line shorted to ground or an internally shorted sensor looks to the module like an overheated actuator.",["Signal wire shorted to ground (chafed at the cylinder head)","Sensor shorted internally","Actuator really overheated by a sluggish phaser"],["Check engine light on","Intake phasing on bank 1 limited, less pulling power"],2,3,["P34A4","P34A5","P34A7","P34AA","P34B6"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1)"],P34A7:["A Camshaft Position Actuator Temperature Sensor Circuit High Bank 1","P34A7 is set when the temperature sensor of intake camshaft actuator A on bank 1 delivers a voltage above its upper limit. Most often the sensor wire or its ground is interrupted, or the signal touches a supply voltage; with an NTC-type sensor this reads as an implausibly cold actuator. The module then lacks a usable value for its thermal protection and usually switches to a cautious phasing strategy.",["Signal or ground wire of the sensor interrupted","Signal wire shorted to a supply voltage","Sensor open internally"],["Check engine light on","Intake phasing on bank 1 reduced","Mostly no noticeable effect while driving"],2,3,["P34A4","P34A5","P34A6","P34AB","P34B7"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1)"],P34A8:["A Camshaft Position Actuator Temperature Sensor Circuit Bank 2","P34A8 mirrors P34A4 on bank 2: the module detects an open or otherwise faulty circuit at the temperature sensor of intake cam actuator A on the side without cylinder 1. Only V and boxer engines have this bank.",["Plug at the bank 2 actuator corroded or not latched","Harness chafed near the cylinder head","Temperature sensor failed"],["Check engine light on","Intake phasing on bank 2 restricted"],2,3,["P34A9","P34AA","P34AB","P34A4","P34B8"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 2)"],P34A9:["A Camshaft Position Actuator Temperature Sensor Range/Performance Bank 2","P34A9 covers the plausibility check of the temperature sensor at intake cam actuator A on bank 2. Nissan names it together with P34A5 in bulletins NTB18-016 (2018 Pathfinder) and ITB18-009 (2018 QX60): vehicles built before 18 December 2017 could store one or both codes and switch on the MIL when started in freezing weather.",["Module software (Nissan 2018 Pathfinder/QX60, reprogramming)","Sensor reading wandering or slow","Poor contact at the bank 2 actuator plug"],["Check engine light on after a start in freezing weather","Engine runs normally in most cases"],2,3,["P34A8","P34AA","P34AB","P34A5","P0021"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 2)"],P34AA:["A Camshaft Position Actuator Temperature Sensor Circuit Low Bank 2","P34AA reports that the temperature sensor of the bank 2 intake cam actuator signals a voltage below its permitted range. Whether that equals a hot reading depends on the sensor design, which no public source names; with the common NTC thermistor it would mimic overheating, and the controller could limit the actuator current or stop phasing on that bank.",["Signal wire grounded against the cylinder head","Cables pinched during earlier engine work","Sensor shorted internally"],["Check engine light on","Intake phasing on bank 2 suspended, slightly less power"],2,3,["P34A8","P34A9","P34AB","P34A6","P34BA"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 2)"],P34AB:["A Camshaft Position Actuator Temperature Sensor Circuit High Bank 2","P34AB stands for a voltage above the upper limit at the temperature sensor of intake cam actuator A, bank 2. An interrupted signal or ground line is the classic cause, as is a short to a higher voltage; a plug pushed off during a service visit often explains it.",["Plug at the actuator off or not latched after service","Signal or ground wire interrupted","Signal shorted to a higher voltage"],["Check engine light on","Intake phasing on bank 2 held back"],2,3,["P34A8","P34A9","P34AA","P34A7","P34BB"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 2)"],P34AC:["A Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor A Circuit Bank 1","P34AC covers any electrical fault in the circuit of position sensor A of the intake cam actuator on bank 1. On engines with an electric intake phaser this sensor tells the controller where the drive motor stands.",["Actuator harness open or shorted, plug loose","Position sensor in the electric actuator failed (actuator replacement)","Electric valve timing control module faulty"],["Check engine light on","Intake cam held in its base position, less torque at low revs","Rougher cold start, slightly higher consumption"],2,3,["P34AD","P34AE","P34AF","P34B0","P34C8","P2B3F"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 1)"],P34AD:["A Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor A Range/Performance Bank 1","P34AD covers a plausibility fault: the position sensor A signal from the intake actuator on bank 1 is electrically present but does not agree with what else the module knows. On the 2022 Mitsubishi Outlander, which turns its intake phaser electrically, the control module checks the motor position against the phase seen by the intake camshaft sensor and logs P34AD when the two disagree;",["Electric actuator worn, sticking or slipping","Actuator position not relearned after repair","Intake camshaft sensor signal or timing drive disturbed","Intermittent wiring fault"],["Check engine light on","Intake cam timing fixed, weaker response at low revs","Possibly accompanying timing codes such as P0011"],3,3,["P34AC","P34AE","P34AF","P34B1","P0011","P2B40"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 1)"],P34AE:["A Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor A Circuit Low Bank 1","P34AE says the voltage from position sensor A on the bank 1 intake side remains under its minimum. The 2022 Mitsubishi Outlander, whose intake cam is moved by an electric motor, evaluates the code in the electric valve timing module and points to an open or shorted actuator circuit or a faulty actuator; unlike the circuit and high codes, no delay time is stated.",["Signal line shorted to ground","Sensor supply open or shorted","Hall sensor in the actuator motor shorted (actuator replacement)"],["Check engine light on","Less pulling power at low revs","Rougher running after a cold start"],2,3,["P34AC","P34AD","P34AF","P34B2","P2B41"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1)"],P34AF:["A Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor A Circuit High Bank 1","P34AF is logged when position sensor A on the bank 1 intake phaser reports a voltage above its upper limit for at least one second. Mitsubishi covers the code in its 2022 Outlander manual and, besides the harness, points to the Hall sensor of motor 1 in the electric actuator – a hint that position sensor A is a Hall element inside the phaser motor.",["Sensor ground open or plug corroded","Signal wire shorted to supply voltage","Hall sensor of the actuator motor failed (actuator replacement)"],["Check engine light on","Intake phaser held in its base position, reduced power","Slightly higher fuel consumption"],2,3,["P34AC","P34AD","P34AE","P34B3","P2B42"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1)"],P34B0:["A Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor A Circuit Bank 2","P34B0 concerns the electrical circuit of position sensor A of the intake cam actuator on bank 2, so it only concerns V and boxer engines. No manufacturer publishes it. Mitsubishi documents the bank 1 code P34AC for the 2022 Outlander, which uses only the bank 1 codes: there the sensor reports the angle of the electric phaser motor, and a voltage outside its window for a second sets the fault.",["Plug or harness to the bank 2 actuator open or shorted","Position sensor in the actuator failed","Control module fault"],["Check engine light on","Bank 2 intake phasing held in its base position","Possibly less power and uneven running between banks"],2,3,["P34B1","P34B2","P34B3","P34AC","P2B43"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 2)"],P34B1:["A Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor A Range/Performance Bank 2","P34B1 means the intake-side position sensor A of bank 2 delivers an electrically sound but implausible value. No public manufacturer document uses this code. The nearest published example is the bank 1 code P34AD on the 2022 Mitsubishi Outlander, where the electric phaser module checks the motor position against the intake camshaft sensor and flags a mismatch.",["Actuator on bank 2 sticking or worn","Learned actuator position lost or software outdated","Bank 2 intake camshaft signal disturbed"],["Check engine light on","Bank 2 intake timing fixed, reduced power","Possibly further timing codes such as P0021"],3,3,["P34B0","P34B2","P34B3","P34AD","P0021","P2B44"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 2)"],P34B2:["A Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor A Circuit Low Bank 2","P34B2 is set when position sensor A on the intake phaser of bank 2 delivers a voltage below its permitted window. Public manufacturer information on this code is lacking. On the 2022 Mitsubishi Outlander the bank 1 version P34AE is evaluated by the electric valve timing module and traced to the actuator circuit or the actuator.",["Signal wire grounded, harness heat-damaged","Sensor supply interrupted","Sensor in the actuator shorted"],["Check engine light on","Bank 2 intake phasing switched off","Possibly codes from other sensors on the same supply"],2,3,["P34B0","P34B1","P34B3","P34AE","P2B45"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 2)"],P34B3:["A Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor A Circuit High Bank 2","P34B3 marks a signal above the upper limit from position sensor A on the intake phaser of bank 2. An interrupted ground, a signal wire touching a supply voltage or a worn-out sensor are the usual findings. No carmaker publishes the code.",["Sensor ground interrupted","Signal wire touching a supply voltage","Hall sensor in the actuator defective (actuator replacement)"],["Check engine light on","Bank 2 intake phaser held at its base angle"],2,3,["P34B0","P34B1","P34B2","P34AF","P2B46"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 2)"],P34B4:["B Camshaft Position Actuator Temperature Sensor Circuit Bank 1","P34B4 reports that the circuit of the temperature sensor on camshaft actuator B, bank 1, cannot be evaluated: an open line, a disconnected plug or a reading that fits no valid state. In the supplier list of NTN-SNR the letter B stands for the outlet camshaft, so the code targets an exhaust phaser turned by an electric motor whose electronics need heat protection.",["Plug at the exhaust actuator not seated or wire broken","Temperature sensor in the actuator electronics failed","Faulty input stage in the controlling module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp lit","Exhaust cam timing on bank 1 fixed or limited","Driving usually unaffected"],2,3,["P34B5","P34B6","P34B7","P34B8","P34A4","P34C8"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 1)"],P34B5:["B Camshaft Position Actuator Temperature Sensor Range/Performance Bank 1","P34B5 is the rationality check for the temperature reading of exhaust-side actuator B on bank 1: the circuit is intact, yet the value or its behaviour is not believable. CARB asks for such checks on VVT input sensors wherever feasible, ideally catching readings that are wrongly high as well as wrongly low. How a carmaker judges this reading is not public, and no maker publishes P34B5 at all.",["Module software judging the value wrongly (update available?)","Temperature sensor in the actuator drifting","Loose contact shifting the reading"],["Malfunction indicator lamp, sometimes only after a cold start","No noticeable change in engine behaviour in most cases"],2,3,["P34B4","P34B6","P34B7","P34B9","P34A5"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 1)"],P34B6:["B Camshaft Position Actuator Temperature Sensor Circuit Low Bank 1","Circuit Low means the voltage on the signal wire of the exhaust actuator B temperature sensor (bank 1) stays under its lower limit. Which temperature that stands for depends on a sensor curve that no public source gives; with a thermistor whose resistance falls as it warms, a short to ground would look like extreme heat.",["Signal wire chafed through and touching ground","Sensor element shorted inside the actuator","Actuator driver genuinely overheated by a binding phaser"],["Malfunction indicator lamp lit","Exhaust phasing on bank 1 reduced, slightly rougher idle possible"],2,3,["P34B4","P34B5","P34B7","P34BA","P34A6"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1)"],P34B7:["B Camshaft Position Actuator Temperature Sensor Circuit High Bank 1","P34B7 sets when the heat reading delivered by exhaust actuator B, bank 1, sits above its upper limit. Electrically this points to an open signal line, a detached sensor ground or contact with battery or reference voltage; with a negative-coefficient element the module would see an implausibly cold actuator.",["Signal line or sensor ground interrupted, plug corroded","Signal line shorted to a supply wire","Sensor element open inside the actuator"],["Malfunction indicator lamp lit","Exhaust cam on bank 1 held in its default position"],2,3,["P34B4","P34B5","P34B6","P34BB","P34A7"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1)"],P34B8:["B Camshaft Position Actuator Temperature Sensor Circuit Bank 2","P34B8 is the circuit fault for the heat sensor inside exhaust camshaft actuator B of bank 2, the row without cylinder 1 on a V or flat engine. If P34B4 is stored at the same time, a shared feed, a common ground or the control module is more likely than two failed sensors at once.",["Connector or harness at the bank 2 exhaust actuator open","Shared supply or ground faulty (when bank 1 also reports)","Temperature sensor in the bank 2 actuator failed"],["Malfunction indicator lamp lit","Exhaust phasing on bank 2 restricted, banks may run slightly unevenly"],2,3,["P34B4","P34B9","P34BA","P34BB","P34A8"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 2)"],P34B9:["B Camshaft Position Actuator Temperature Sensor Range/Performance Bank 2","With P34B9 the bank 2 exhaust actuator reports a temperature that is electrically valid but does not make sense. A two-bank engine offers an obvious yardstick: after a long cold soak both exhaust actuators should read almost the same, and under equal load they should warm alike. Whether any carmaker applies such logic to P34B9 is not published; the code appears only in lists such as the one from NTN-SNR.",["Bank 2 actuator temperature sensor drifting","Contact resistance at the plug shifting the value","Module software outdated"],["Malfunction indicator lamp lit","Usually no change in driveability"],2,3,["P34B5","P34B8","P34BA","P34BB","P34A9"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 2)"],P34BA:["B Camshaft Position Actuator Temperature Sensor Circuit Low Bank 2","P34BA tells that the temperature signal from bank 2's exhaust actuator is pulled under its lower limit. Typical sources are a signal wire that has found ground, for instance where the harness runs close to hot exhaust parts, or a sensor element shorted inside the actuator.",["Harness near exhaust parts damaged, signal shorted to ground","Sensor element shorted inside the bank 2 actuator","Input of the controlling module faulty"],["Malfunction indicator lamp lit","Bank 2 exhaust timing limited, possibly with additional timing codes"],2,3,["P34B6","P34B8","P34B9","P34BB","P0024"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 2)"],P34BB:["B Camshaft Position Actuator Temperature Sensor Circuit High Bank 2","P34BB is stored when the bank 2 exhaust actuator's temperature signal stays above its window – typically a broken signal line, a loosened ground connection or contact with a supply wire. Because the module can no longer see how warm the actuator driver is, it lacks what it needs to protect it;",["Signal line broken or sensor ground loose","Signal line touching a supply wire","Sensor open inside the bank 2 actuator"],["Malfunction indicator lamp lit","Bank 2 exhaust cam held in a safe position"],2,3,["P34B7","P34B8","P34B9","P34BA","P34AB"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 2)"],P34BC:["B Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor A Circuit Bank 1","P34BC means the module cannot make sense of the wiring of sensor A, which reports where actuator B on bank 1 stands. Read against the NTN-SNR list, actuator B is the exhaust-side one. Where such actuators are electric, sensor A reports the motor or phaser angle; Mitsubishi shows the intake equivalent P34AC, set after a voltage outside the window for one second or more.",["Connector at the exhaust actuator unplugged or corroded, wire broken","Sensor supply or ground missing","Sensor integrated in the actuator failed (actuator replacement)"],["Malfunction indicator lamp lit","Exhaust-side adjustment on bank 1 switched off","Possibly slightly higher fuel consumption"],2,3,["P34BD","P34BE","P34BF","P34C0","P34AC","P2B47"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 1)"],P34BD:["B Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor A Range/Performance Bank 1","P34BD has a documented user. Mercedes-Benz lists P34BD09 in bulletin LI05.20-P-080192, dated 14 January 2026, for M176/M177 V8 engines with CAMTRONIC, used for example in the AMG C 63 and E 63, the G 550 and the Maybach GLS 600. Its fault text reports the feedback from exhaust-side CAMTRONIC solenoid 1 of bank 1 as faulty and classes it as a component fault.",["Engine control software outdated (Mercedes M176/M177: update)","CAMTRONIC actuator of a superseded part number","Harness heat-damaged above the bulkhead"],["Check engine light on","CAMTRONIC in limp-home mode, often with further CAMTRONIC codes"],3,3,["P34BC","P34BE","P34BF","P34C1","P005A","P2B48"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 1)"],P34BE:["B Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor A Circuit Low Bank 1","For P34BE, too, a Mercedes-Benz text exists: the CAMTRONIC bulletin covering the M176 and M177 eight-cylinders reads P34BE00 as the signal of exhaust solenoid 1, bank 1, being grounded. That fits the generic meaning, a signal under its lower limit. Mercedes points to the engine cover and the wiring routed over the bulkhead, close to the windshield, where heat damage was found;",["Heat-damaged harness above the bulkhead, signal shorted to ground","Sensor inside the CAMTRONIC actuator shorted (older part number)","Engine control software not up to date"],["Check engine light on","CAMTRONIC limp-home, exhaust valve lift on bank 1 no longer switched"],3,3,["P34BC","P34BD","P34BF","P34C2","P2B49"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1)"],P34BF:["B Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor A Circuit High Bank 1","P34BF: on bank 1, sensor A of the camshaft B actuator, i.e. the exhaust side, sends more voltage than allowed. An open ground, a signal wire in contact with a feed or an internally open sensor are the usual explanations. Mercedes-Benz documents low and implausible signals for this sensor on its CAMTRONIC V8 (P34BE, P34BD), but no high fault; other manufacturers do not mention the code either.",["Sensor ground interrupted or plug corroded","Signal line shorted to a supply wire","Sensor in the exhaust actuator open internally"],["Malfunction indicator lamp lit","Exhaust adjustment on bank 1 kept in its reference position"],2,3,["P34BC","P34BD","P34BE","P34C3","P34AF","P2B4A"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1)"],P34C0:["B Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor A Circuit Bank 2","P34C0 is the generic circuit fault of position sensor A belonging to camshaft actuator B of bank 2 and therefore appears only on V-type or other two-bank engines. Mercedes-Benz files the bank 2 exhaust feedback of its CAMTRONIC V8 (M176/M177) under neighbouring codes – P34C1 for an implausible signal, P34C2 for a grounded one – but P34C0 itself is absent from its bulletin, and no other carmaker has published it.",["Wiring or plug at the bank 2 exhaust actuator open","Shared sensor feed or ground faulty (if P34BC is also stored)","Sensor in the bank 2 actuator failed"],["Malfunction indicator lamp lit","Exhaust adjustment on bank 2 disabled"],2,3,["P34BC","P34C1","P34C2","P34C3","P34B0","P2B4B"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 2)"],P34C1:["B Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor A Range/Performance Bank 2","Mercedes-Benz names P34C109 for the exhaust side of bank 2 on its CAMTRONIC V8s: the signal from the sensor at solenoid 1 is wrong although the circuit is intact, entered as a component fault. CARB explains why such a check exists, since even a single cylinder pin on a lift mechanism not moving into place is a failure mode that VVT monitoring has to cover.",["CAMTRONIC actuator of an older part number (Mercedes: replace)","Engine control software needs an update","Actuator pin sticking or moving too slowly"],["Check engine light on","CAMTRONIC limp-home, often together with P005C"],3,3,["P34BD","P34C0","P34C2","P34C3","P005C","P2B4C"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 2)"],P34C2:["B Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor A Circuit Low Bank 2","Mercedes-Benz documents this code as P34C200: on cylinder bank 2, the feedback line of CAMTRONIC exhaust solenoid 1 is grounded. The code is one of sixteen that bulletin LI05.20-P-080192 groups together for engine types M176 and M177, found in AMG 63 models as well as S-Class, G-Class and GLS cars.",["Harness near the windshield heat-damaged, signal to ground","Sensor in the bank 2 CAMTRONIC actuator shorted","Engine control software outdated"],["Check engine light on","CAMTRONIC limp-home, exhaust lift on bank 2 fixed"],3,3,["P34BE","P34C0","P34C1","P34C3","P2B4D"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 2)"],P34C3:["B Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor A Circuit High Bank 2","P34C3 completes the sensor group of actuator B: on bank 2, sensor A watching the exhaust-side actuator puts out a voltage beyond its permitted range. A broken sensor ground, an open signal path or contact with a feed line are the usual causes. No manufacturer publishes P34C3.",["Sensor ground on bank 2 broken","Signal line in contact with a supply wire","Sensor in the bank 2 exhaust actuator faulty"],["Malfunction indicator lamp lit","Bank 2 exhaust adjustment held in base position"],2,3,["P34BF","P34C0","P34C1","P34C2","P34B3","P2B4E"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 2)"],P34C4:["A Camshaft Position Actuator Control Circuit Driver Current/Temperature Too High Bank 1","P34C4 is logged when the output stage feeding the bank 1 intake actuator A reports that its current or its own temperature has passed the permitted limit. The code belongs to electric phasers, where a small motor instead of an oil valve turns the camshaft.",["Phaser stiff or held against its stop, motor draws high current for long","Low or sludged engine oil making the phaser hard to turn","Winding or motor lead of the bank 1 actuator shorted","Output stage or its sensors in the phaser control module faulty"],["Check engine light on","Intake timing on bank 1 no longer adjusted, held at a fixed angle","Weaker pull at low revs, rougher idle on a cold engine"],3,3,["P34C5","P34C6","P34C8","P34A4","P34AC","P0010"],"מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A — זרם או חום גבוהים מדי בדרייבר של מעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P34C5:["A Camshaft Position Actuator Control Circuit Driver Current/Temperature Too High Bank 2","P34C5 mirrors P34C4 on bank 2 for intake actuator A: the driver powering the electric phaser motor on the second cylinder bank has measured too much current or run too hot and protects itself. Only V or boxer engines with one electric intake phaser per bank can log it. Two banks give a handy cross-check: if the fault stays on bank 2 after the motors trade places, wiring or the module are to blame;",["Bank 2 phaser stiff or stuck at an end stop","Motor lead to the bank 2 actuator chafed or shorted","Electric motor of the bank 2 actuator worn or internally shorted","Bank 2 output stage in the phaser control module faulty"],["Check engine light on","Bank 2 intake timing frozen, banks run unevenly","Slightly rough idle and less torque at low engine speed"],3,3,["P34C4","P34C7","P34C8","P34A8","P34A9","P0020"],"מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A — זרם או חום גבוהים מדי בדרייבר של מעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P34C6:["B Camshaft Position Actuator Control Circuit Driver Current/Temperature Too High Bank 1","P34C6 concerns actuator B, which NTN-SNR assigns to the exhaust camshaft, on bank 1: the stage driving it signals overcurrent or overheating. That presumes an electrically powered exhaust phaser, and none is documented in public sources.",["Exhaust phaser on bank 1 stiff, motor overloaded","Short in the motor wiring of actuator B, bank 1","Output stage for actuator B damaged or overheated"],["Check engine light on","Exhaust cam timing on bank 1 fixed in its default position","Slightly higher fuel use, minor loss of smoothness"],3,3,["P34C7","P34C4","P34C8","P34B4","P34BC","P0013"],"מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B — זרם או חום גבוהים מדי בדרייבר של מעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P34C7:["B Camshaft Position Actuator Control Circuit Driver Current/Temperature Too High Bank 2","P34C7 closes the group of four driver-load codes: on bank 2 the power stage of the exhaust-side actuator B reports current or temperature above its limit. NTN-SNR ties it to outlet adjustment on the second bank. It is the rarest of the set, because electric phasers have so far appeared on the intake side; no public manufacturer document names P34C7.",["Bank 2 exhaust phaser seized or poorly lubricated","Motor wiring of actuator B, bank 2, shorted or heat-damaged","Driver overheating from poor cooling or a module fault"],["Check engine light on","Bank 2 exhaust timing no longer varied","Usually only small changes in how the engine runs"],3,3,["P34C6","P34C5","P34C8","P34B8","P34C0","P0023"],"מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B — זרם או חום גבוהים מדי בדרייבר של מעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P34C8:["Camshaft Position Control Module Performance","P34C8 does not point at one actuator or bank; it says the separate controller for cam adjustment is not working properly in itself. Mitsubishi defines it for the 2022 Outlander: with the ignition on, the controller of the electric intake phaser detects an internal CPU error, and the module is the only listed cause.",["Internal processor fault in the cam adjustment control module","Outdated control software (Mercedes M176/M177: update)","Module supply or harness heat-damaged or with poor contact"],["Check engine light on","Cam phasing held at its reference position","Rougher cold start and fixed idle speed","Noticeably less torque, higher fuel use"],2,3,["P34C4","P34C5","P34C6","P34C7","P0606","P34AC"],"מודול בקרת מצב גל זיזים — ביצועים לא תקינים"]};export{e as default};
